{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T00:49:27.465Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a2eacd3e6f1c77635</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LCuXRjFFdmBCNzCiS2VmCp</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/5e79b5c6-5688-4728-8d81-ff2c106a0e2e/tasks/a2eacd3e6f1c77635.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement TASK-08 (AC-05b regression test)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**TASK-08** (AC-05b regression-proof test) is done.\n\n- Read AC-05b from `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK3A-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP.json` on disk before writing the test — criterion confirmed: root has no `Cargo.toml` at all, `crates/kept/Cargo.toml` elsewhere must still be admitted as `Ecosystem::Cargo`, treated identically to AC-05 (no filter, not zero admitted, no error).\n- Added `ac05b_admits_cargo_candidates_when_root_has_no_cargo_toml_file_at_all` at `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs:400`.\n- Ran it first: it passed immediately (matching TASK-07's precedent — the fallback logic already exists from TASK-03a/TASK-05, no code path was missing). Rather than trust that characterization, I adversarially broke `read_cargo_membership`'s `Err(_)` branch at `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs:86` (temporarily forcing `members: Some(empty)` instead of `absent_cargo_membership()`), reran, and confirmed the test genuinely fails (`crates/kept must be admitted as Cargo, got: []`) — proving the test isn't vacuous. Reverted the sabotage, reran, confirmed green again.\n- Full suite: `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib` → 279 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph` — no changes needed. `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` — clean.\n- Committed as `498f27c`, pre-commit format-check hook passed.\n- No precision_tests were supplied for this task.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-08\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"read_spec_criterion_AC-05b\",\n    \"wrote_failing_test\",\n    \"confirmed_test_passed_immediately\",\n    \"adversarially_verified_test_is_not_vacuous_by_breaking_and_restoring_fallback\",\n    \"ran_full_lib_suite_green\",\n    \"cargo_fmt\",\n    \"cargo_clippy_clean\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"498f27c\",\n  \"concerns\": \"No red-phase existed on the actual task diff, matching the TASK-07 precedent noted in the plan: the Cargo.toml-absent fallback (Err(_) =&gt; absent_cargo_membership()) was already implemented and wired by TASK-03a/TASK-05. Honesty was preserved by adversarially breaking that fallback and confirming the new test fails without it, then restoring it, rather than assuming the plan's 'no red step' note was correct.\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-05b\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 400,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 86\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>62755</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>34</tool_uses><duration_ms>745809</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
