{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T01:51:08.023Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae132688a124c912f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/5e79b5c6-5688-4728-8d81-ff2c106a0e2e/tasks/ae132688a124c912f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement TASK-17 (AC-10b regression test)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Committed successfully as `98cb1e2`. Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\n**TASK-17: Regression-proof AC-10b (pnpm empty packages list excludes everything)**\n\n- Confirmed pre-state: all 12 prior commits (0971005…c98ae29) present on `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs`, tree clean before starting.\n- Read AC-10b's exact text from `.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK3A-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP.json` on disk. The spec text includes an explicit hybrid-root exemption clause the plan's single fixture did not cover, so I added a second test to fully prove the criterion as written, per the established pattern from TASK-12/14.\n- Wrote two tests in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs`:\n  - `ac10b_pnpm_empty_packages_list_admits_zero_npm_entries` (line 817) — matches the plan's fixture exactly.\n  - `ac10b_pnpm_empty_packages_list_still_admits_hybrid_root` (line 842) — new, covers the spec's hybrid-root carve-out that the plan's fixture omitted.\n- Both passed immediately (no red step) against the existing implementation — same pattern as TASK-07 through TASK-16.\n- Adversarially verified non-vacuousness by temporarily mutating `NpmMembership::admits` in `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs`:\n  - Removed the `hybrid_root` short-circuit → the hybrid-root test failed as expected.\n  - Made the empty-globset case fall through to admit-all → both tests failed as expected.\n  - Restored the original code (verified `git diff` on membership.rs was empty afterward).\n- Full `callisto-graph` lib suite: 289 passed, 0 failed. `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` both clean.\n- Committed as `98cb1e2`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-17\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"confirmed prior 12 commits present and tree clean\",\n    \"read AC-10b acceptance criterion text directly from spec file on disk\",\n    \"identified plan fixture omitted spec's hybrid-root exemption clause and added a second test to cover it\",\n    \"wrote both tests (red-step check: passed immediately, consistent with prior regression-proof tasks in this range)\",\n    \"adversarially verified non-vacuousness by breaking hybrid_root short-circuit and empty-globset behavior in membership.rs, confirming each test failed appropriately, then restored original code\",\n    \"ran full callisto-graph lib test suite (289 passed)\",\n    \"ran cargo fmt -p callisto-graph and cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"98cb1e2\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-10b\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 817,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 230\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"No genuine red step occurred (consistent with TASK-07 through TASK-16 in this plan); non-vacuousness was verified via adversarial mutation instead, per the task's own instructions. The plan's original fixture only covered the zero-npm-entries half of AC-10b; I added a second test (ac10b_pnpm_empty_packages_list_still_admits_hybrid_root, line 842) to cover the hybrid-root exemption clause explicitly named in the spec's criterion text, which the plan's fixture omitted.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Spec AC-10b text explicitly carves out an AC-17-style hybrid-root exemption from its zero-entries claim. The plan's single fixture (no root package.json) never exercises that carve-out, so a literal reading of the plan alone would under-prove the criterion. Added a second fixture with a root package.json declaring 'name' to prove the exemption holds. Verified both tests are meaningful via targeted mutation of NpmMembership::admits before committing.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>85136</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>505568</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
