": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 104\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"This task's plan fixture only tested the bare-string exclude case. AC-09b's exact spec text (last sentence) also requires 'an exclude array containing one or more non-string entries' to be treated identically. Added ac09b_malformed_cargo_exclude_non_string_entry_falls_back_to_excluding_nothing to close that gap in the ignore_walk.rs-level integration coverage (the membership.rs unit-level tests already only covered the bare-string variant too, at both layers). Underlying implementation required no changes — the fallback logic in membership.rs's read_cargo_membership (lines 104-108) already handled both malformed shapes correctly via parse_toml_string_array returning None and unwrap_or_else(GlobSet::empty).\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Confirmed via git log that exactly 16 commits (d812cac..ac02058) touch ignore_walk.rs as part of TASK-05..TASK-20, plus one unrelated pre-existing commit (ad019ea). Tree was clean, ahead of origin only. Read AC-09b from the spec file directly rather than trusting plan prose. The plan's failing_test only exercised the bare-string exclude shape; per the recurring pattern noted for TASK-12/14/17/20, added the missing non-string-entries exclude array variant explicitly required by the spec's final sentence. Both tests passed with zero implementation changes needed, consistent with the established regression-proof pattern for TASK-07 through TASK-20. Verified non-vacuousness by temporarily breaking the exclude-fallback unwrap_or_else in membership.rs and confirming both tests failed with assertion panics, then restored it exactly to its original state (git diff shows zero net change to membership.rs).\"\n}\n```\n\nSummary: TASK-21 is done. Added two tests to `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs` — `ac09b_malformed_cargo_exclude_bare_string_falls_back_to_excluding_nothing` (line 1218, matching the plan) and `ac09b_malformed_cargo_exclude_non_string_entry_falls_back_to_excluding_nothing` (line 1259, added because the spec's AC-09b text requires it but the plan's fixture omitted it). No implementation change was needed — `read_cargo_membership` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs` (line 104) already falls back correctly for both malformed shapes. Verified non-vacuous by temporarily breaking the fallback and confirming both tests failed, then restored. Full suite (296 tests), fmt, and clippy all clean. Committed as `686ab58`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>57460</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>346404</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"550216f8-dc54-4a08-a3e5-bbbd15f5b4e0","timestamp":"2026-08-16T02:19:22.618Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.232","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
