hrough TASK-22 just landed changes to (commits 0971005 through 68af77f, 18 commits total, all already on the current branch). Start by running `git log --oneline -19 -- crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs` and `git status` to confirm all eighteen are present and the tree is clean before you begin.\n\nTASK-07 through TASK-22 were all titled \"regression-proof\" and all required no new implementation (behavior already existed from earlier tasks, tests passed immediately). This task may follow the same pattern, or may not — verify by actually running the tests yourself, don't assume either way. If a test passes with no red step, adversarially verify it's not vacuous (temporarily break the relevant logic in membership.rs, confirm the test then fails, then restore it) — this precedent has worked well throughout and should continue.\n\nEstablished patterns from this same plan's ~39 prior completed tasks, still applicable:\n- A recurring gotcha on this plan: task notes/prose (failing_test predictions, \"note\" fields, assumptions about prior task state) have repeatedly diverged from actual observed behavior in earlier tasks. Always verify by actually running the test/command yourself, never trust the plan's characterization blindly.\n- `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` workspace invariant — never introduce unsafe blocks.\n- Run `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph` and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` before committing; this repo's pre-commit hook enforces format-check and WILL reject an unformatted commit — if that happens, run `cargo fmt`, re-stage, and create a fresh commit (do not amend).\n- Watch for `clippy::cmp_owned` specifically if your test compares a `PathBuf` — use `Path::new(\"...\")` on the right-hand side of `==` against a `PathBuf`/`&Path`, not `PathBuf::from(\"...\")`. This lint has bitten prior tasks already.\n- Commit per task once green, using the plan's commit_message (or a corrected one if it doesn't match what was actually i