{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-16T03:11:36.665Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a08f4b0d318eae3d4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01L3oQ83audb9VwyaY15h8WH</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/5e79b5c6-5688-4728-8d81-ff2c106a0e2e/tasks/a08f4b0d318eae3d4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement TASK-29 (AC-11d regression test)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Committed successfully as `d4dd8cc`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**TASK-29** — Regression-proof AC-11d (comments-only pnpm-workspace.yaml → zero YAML documents, no panic)\n\nRead the exact spec text from `.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK3A-WORKSPACE-MEMBERSHIP.json`, which was broader than the plan's paraphrase: AC-11d covers three input shapes that all yield zero YAML documents — **empty (zero bytes)**, **whitespace-only**, and **comments-only** — not just the comments-only case the plan's `failing_test` stub included. I wrote a single test covering all three sub-cases per the \"add anything missing\" guidance.\n\nTest passed immediately (no red step, consistent with the plan's note that this is regression-proofing of already-existing behavior). Since a same-run false green is the exact failure mode this task type risks, I adversarially verified non-vacuousness: temporarily changed `crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs:276` from `docs.first()?` to `&amp;docs[0]`, reran the test, confirmed it genuinely panics (`index out of bounds: the len is 0 but the index is 0`), then restored the original safe code. Full `cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib` (309 tests) passes clean, `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy -p callisto-graph --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"TASK-29\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"confirmed 24 prior commits present on ignore_walk.rs and clean tree\",\n    \"read AC-11d exact criterion text from spec file on disk\",\n    \"wrote test covering all three zero-document input shapes (empty/whitespace/comments)\",\n    \"ran test — passed immediately (no red step, as expected for regression-proof task)\",\n    \"adversarially broke docs.first()? -&gt; docs[0] in membership.rs, confirmed test panics\",\n    \"restored membership.rs to original safe form, confirmed diff clean\",\n    \"ran full callisto-graph lib test suite (309 passed)\",\n    \"ran cargo fmt and cargo clippy -D warnings (clean)\",\n    \"committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"d4dd8cc\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [\n    {\n      \"criterion_id\": \"AC-11d\",\n      \"test_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/ignore_walk.rs\",\n      \"test_line\": 1709,\n      \"implementation_file\": \"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/locate/membership.rs\",\n      \"implementation_line\": 276\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concerns\": \"Plan's failing_test stub only covered the comments-only variant; test was expanded to cover all three zero-document shapes named in AC-11d's exact spec text (empty, whitespace-only, comments-only) per the task instruction to reconcile plan vs spec.\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"No implementation change needed; docs.first()? in membership.rs:276 already guards this case correctly, confirmed via mutation-style adversarial check.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>53518</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>345078</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
