{"parentUuid":"b25989db-11c6-4817-9660-d171fe337c9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8YU3ufENMyTUGjofLvo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have solid grounding for all three sub-issues. Drafting the requirement and dispatching to canon-drafter."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":343517,"output_tokens":3367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":324},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3367,"cache_read_input_tokens":343517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8YTxXxJ7PvEpqptWWAi","type":"assistant","uuid":"ddf2da15-5fcf-45d2-af80-ad20eb672a2a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:17:50.357Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"ddf2da15-5fcf-45d2-af80-ad20eb672a2a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8YU3ufENMyTUGjofLvo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014HpBkekPgXTDPuGXvxqdUi","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Draft Track 1 spec (fixed-group cascade correctness)","subagent_type":"canon:drafter","prompt":"Draft a spec@1 from the following requirement@1 for the callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto. This is \"Track 1\" of a larger, already-approved remediation plan (full plan context below for background only — your job is just this track).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS\",\n  \"statement\": \"Fix three independent, confirmed-live correctness bugs in callisto's fixed-group version engine: (1) fixed-group siblings are bumped independently from their own base version instead of a shared group-aligned target, (2) a fully-implemented divergence/napi-drift pre-mutation check function is never called from any command, and (3) a declared error variant for detecting same-target-different-spelling group membership conflicts is never constructed.\",\n  \"stakeholder\": \"Callisto maintainers and any user with a fixed-group release configuration (napi-rs platform packages, monorepo packages that must always release in lockstep)\",\n  \"why\": \"All three bugs were confirmed live via direct code inspection this session, not just documentation drift. Bug 1 causes silent, permanent version divergence within a group the user explicitly configured to stay in lockstep — the exact failure mode fixed groups exist to prevent. Bugs 2 and 3 are complete, unit-tested implementations sitting completely disconnected from any real command, so their protections silently do not apply to any real `callisto version` run today.\",\n  \"done_when\": [\n    \"Given a Fixed group with two Package members, one already released (has a prior tag) at version 2.0.0 and one never-released at version 0.1.0, and a cascade run that assigns both a Minor severity bump, both siblings' computed target version is the SAME group-aligned version (derived from the released sibling's tag-based version per the existing fixed_group_target function in groups.rs), not two independently-bumped versions computed from each sibling's own divergent base.\",\n    \"This holds through the real, live call path: crate::cascade::run_cascade -> raise() -> the per-sibling fixed-group loop -> bump_target, not just in a unit test of fixed_group_target called directly.\",\n    \"CascadeInput gains a `tags: &TagIndex` field (TagIndex from crate::tags) since fixed_group_target requires it. Both real construction sites are updated: crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:70 and crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs:53. (Correction to prior planning notes: apply.rs / apply_version_plan does NOT construct CascadeInput -- it consumes an already-computed VersionPlan built by version.rs's cascade run. Only these two real sites exist; verify this yourself against current code rather than trusting this claim.)\",\n    \"Explicit decision, stated in the spec (not left ambiguous): whether commands/snapshot.rs's fixed-group target computation is brought into scope by this same fix (since it constructs its own CascadeInput and would otherwise silently diverge from version.rs's corrected behavior) or is explicitly out of scope with a stated reason. Do not let this happen as a silent side effect either way.\",\n    \"crate::groups::pre_mutation_checks (groups.rs, fully implemented, unit-tested, already re-exported from lib.rs) is called from commands/version.rs's real orchestration path, before run_cascade executes, using the same GroupTable/base_versions/TagIndex/NapiTargetsIndex it already has in scope at that point in the function.\",\n    \"pre_mutation_checks's return value is actually consumed: GroupCheckOutcome.diagnostics are merged into the command's real diagnostic output (the existing diagnostics collection/output path used elsewhere in version.rs), and a divergence error (GraphError::FixedGroupDivergent / GraphError::GroupGrammarMismatch, both already returned by pre_mutation_checks) actually aborts the version command with that error rather than being silently discarded.\",\n    \"GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership (declared in crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs, currently zero construction sites anywhere) is constructed by new detection logic in GroupTable::resolve (crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs, private fn resolve at line 135) or an equivalent post-resolution check: given two group definitions where a group-member string is spelled differently in each group's raw TOML config (e.g. one group lists \\\"my-lib\\\" and another lists \\\"cargo:my-lib\\\") but both resolve, after identity resolution, to the same real PackageId, GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership is returned identifying both groups and the shared resolved id -- this must NOT happen for the ordinary, allowed case of the same PackageId legitimately belonging to only one group (only for the specific bug case of two DIFFERENT groups both claiming the same resolved package).\",\n    \"Given a workspace config with no group spelling conflicts, GroupTable::resolve behaves exactly as it does today (regression: existing group-resolution tests must all still pass unmodified).\",\n    \"All three fixes are covered by tests that exercise the REAL call path (run_cascade / the version command's real orchestration / GroupTable::resolve), not just isolated unit tests of the already-existing helper functions (fixed_group_target and pre_mutation_checks already have their own isolated unit tests today -- the gap this spec closes is that nothing calls them for real).\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"Track 2 (platform-manifest / optionalDependencies writes) -- separate track, depends on this one, not addressed here.\",\n    \"Track 9 (cascade_action peer-escalation severity bug, dependency-spec rewrite key bug) -- separate, scoped track sharing cascade.rs, sequenced immediately after this one, not part of this spec.\",\n    \"Any change to fixed_group_target's or pre_mutation_checks's own internal logic/signature beyond what's needed to call them from real code -- both are already correct and unit-tested; this track is about wiring, not redesigning them.\",\n    \"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities and error paths beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection -- do not refactor unrelated parts of resolve() as a side effect.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n# Full remediation-plan context for Track 1 (background only, do not exceed this track's scope)\n\nTrack 1 is Phase 1 of a 12-track plan, sequenced immediately after Track 3 (already fully complete: workspace-membership filtering + identity/ecosystem resolution hardening, both shipped and merged this session). Track 1 in turn blocks Track 2 (platform-manifest writes) and is sequenced immediately before Track 9 (a separate, narrower cascade.rs fix for peer-escalation severity and cross-ecosystem rewrite keys -- Track 9 is NOT part of this spec, just sequenced adjacent to it since it shares cascade.rs).\n\nCritical files: crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs (fixed_group_target, pre_mutation_checks -- both already implemented), crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs (GroupTable::resolve -- different file from groups.rs, same basename, do not conflate), crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs (CascadeInput, raise(), bump_target()), crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/{version,snapshot}.rs.\n\nThis repo's established process (see .claude/plans/ACTIVE.md for precedent from Track B/E/F/G/Spec A/Spec B): full canon -> vector -> lambda pipeline for a track like this. `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` is a hard workspace invariant. `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` is mandatory CI. This session's established pattern throughout Track 3's 45-task implementation: acceptance criteria and test fixtures must be verified against the REAL current code before being trusted, since planning documents (including this very requirement) have repeatedly been found to contain small inaccuracies that need correcting during implementation -- treat every code-location/line-number claim above as a starting point to verify, not a fact to trust blindly.\n\nProduce a spec@1 with purpose, scope, non_goals (at least the four out_of_scope items above, stated as non_goals), acceptance_criteria (testable propositions, error cases marked is_error_case: true), and an api_surface section if the fix introduces or changes any public/pub(crate) function signature (CascadeInput gaining a field is exactly such a change -- document it explicitly)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":343517,"output_tokens":3367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":324},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3367,"cache_read_input_tokens":343517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8YTxXxJ7PvEpqptWWAi","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f984883-60b3-4719-bcd3-82b9fe9b2321","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:18:23.753Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
