{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:50:15.903Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a0bfbff13f23340f7</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a0bfbff13f23340f7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Draft Track 1 spec (fixed-group cascade correctness)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Note: claude-sonnet-5[1m] (the safety classifier) was unavailable (timed out) when reviewing this subagent's work. Please carefully verify the subagent's actions and output before acting on them.\n\nThe spec draft is complete. The drafting agent verified every code-location claim in the requirement against the actual current code and corrected several inaccuracies along the way:\n\n**Corrections found during verification:**\n- `fixed_group_target` has **zero** pre-existing unit tests (only `pre_mutation_checks` does) — the requirement's claim that both were \"already unit-tested\" was wrong.\n- `version.rs`'s `plan_version` does **not** already have `TagIndex`/`NapiTargetsIndex` bound in scope as the requirement assumed — `ws.tags()?` is currently called inline unbound, and no `NapiTargetsIndex` is constructed anywhere in that function today. Both now need new local bindings.\n- `CascadeInput` construction sites and line numbers (`version.rs:70`, `snapshot.rs:53`) were confirmed exact; `apply.rs` confirmed to construct neither.\n- `raise()`'s per-sibling fixed-group loop is **shared code** between the version and snapshot call paths, so the bug-1 fix necessarily applies to both commands — while `pre_mutation_checks` wiring is version.rs-only, with an explicit, stated reason (snapshot assigns every package an identical synthetic version, so there's nothing for the divergence check to catch).\n- `GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership`'s exact field shape confirmed as `{ package: PackageId, groups: Vec&lt;GroupName&gt; }`.\n\n**Key spec decisions made explicit (not left ambiguous):**\n- AC-006 + a dedicated non-goal state precisely why `pre_mutation_checks` is *not* wired into `snapshot.rs`, with the technical reason spelled out.\n- AC-004/AC-005 separate \"the shared-target fix applies to snapshot's call path too\" from \"but it doesn't change snapshot's observable output\" — two distinct, both-necessary criteria.\n- 13 acceptance criteria total, 2 marked `is_error_case: true` (the divergence-abort case, the conflicting-membership case), covering all three bugs through their real call paths per the requirement's explicit demand.\n\nThe spec@1 JSON is in the notification above (id `SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS`), and a working copy is saved at:\n`/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json`\n\nThis has **not yet** gone through canon's verify/audit/exit-gate pipeline, and `spec_file_path` has not been set (per this session's established process, that happens after the gate, before handing off to `vector` for implementation planning). Let me know if you'd like me to run the canon gate on it now, or if you want to review/adjust the draft first.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>42673</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>2</tool_uses><duration_ms>722631</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
