006/009/012 are direct restatements or necessary consequences of explicit done_when items. AC-007 and AC-010b have a supported core (abort-on-divergence; cross-group-conflict detection) but add specific mechanism/scope details (named error variants, grammar-mismatch branch, cross-kind unification) with no textual basis, so classified overfitted rather than fully supported. AC-004, AC-007b, and AC-010c were checked hardest since AC-004 and AC-010c both trace to revision_note blockers (BLK-02, BLK-03) added to satisfy a prior canon-exit-gate retry rather than the original requirement — the revision process fixed internal-consistency problems in the spec but in doing so introduced criteria whose justification is 'the exit-gate demanded it' rather than 'the requirement demanded it.' AC-010c is particularly notable: it plausibly conflicts with requirement's own out_of_scope item 4 rather than merely lacking support.\"\n}\n```\n\nNotably, three criteria (AC-004, AC-007b, AC-010c) trace their origin to the prior canon-exit-gate's blocker list (BLK-02, BLK-03 per the spec's `revision_note`) rather than to the source requirement — they were added to close internal-consistency gaps the exit-gate found, not because the requirement called for them. AC-010c in particular appears to sit in tension with `requirement@1`'s own `out_of_scope` boundary (\"GroupTable::resolve's other existing responsibilities... beyond the new ConflictingGroupMembership detection\"). These are flagged above for the auditor/exit-gate to weigh — no verdict issued here.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>60476</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>2</tool_uses><duration_ms>367839</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"ff67a8b4-c132-4b8b-b81a-b4020a818669","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:20:28.142Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d