logic gains two changes: (1) cross-group conflict detection: while building the fixed_of/linked_of maps (currently populated via unchecked .insert() calls at lines 149 and 180 that silently overwrite an existing entry), if a PackageId being inserted for group G2 already has an entry recorded for a different group G1, resolve() returns Err(GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }) where `package` is the shared resolved PackageId and `groups` lists the conflicting group names (at least G1 and G2), instead of completing the insert and returning Ok. Conflict detection is unified across group kinds: a single resolved PackageId may appear in at most one group total (Fixed or Linked), not one-per-kind. The check compares against a single combined view of both fixed_of and linked_of when performing the insert, not two independently-scoped maps. (2) within-group dedup: immediately after the existing `members.sort()` calls (line 164 for the fixed loop, line 195 for the linked loop), add `members.dedup()` so that a PackageId reachable under two different spellings within that one group's own raw member list (e.g. \"my-lib\" and \"cargo:my-lib\" both resolving to the same PackageId) appears exactly once in the resulting GroupDef.members, since `Vec::dedup()` only removes *consecutive* duplicates and the preceding `.sort()` (which sorts GroupMember by its derived Ord, placing equal resolved-PackageId Package members adjacent to each other) guarantees any such duplicate is consecutive before dedup runs. A duplicate spelling of the same PackageId within one group's own membership list is not a cross-group conflict (see AC-010c) — it is handled entirely by this within-group dedup step, which runs before the cross-group conflict check would ever see the second occurrence.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8204e9ca-b6ab-4407-a6a5-c1de9e38382b","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","use