{"parentUuid":"88f70606-2f46-4366-80dd-3bba7fe40663","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8fD8A3b5FwQk1AD1GrS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EaaFiZ6QqeWpHL3BCZGjWc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track1-draft.json') as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\nprint('=== purpose ===')\nprint(d.get('purpose'))\nprint()\nprint('=== revision_note ===')\nprint(d.get('revision_note'))\n\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1912,"cache_read_input_tokens":423536,"output_tokens":971,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":672},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1912,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":971,"cache_read_input_tokens":423536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1912},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8fD5DC7X5krxJYjfYPH","type":"assistant","uuid":"d3bcaf4a-417d-4e36-bd0e-ec2ac4704030","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:46:22.493Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"d3bcaf4a-417d-4e36-bd0e-ec2ac4704030","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"daa78fe3-695a-438e-aed6-d41775edc067","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EaaFiZ6QqeWpHL3BCZGjWc","type":"tool_result","content":"=== purpose ===\nWire three already-implemented but currently disconnected/broken pieces of callisto's fixed-group version engine into the real command call paths: (1) make fixed-group siblings converge on a single shared group-aligned target version instead of each bumping independently from its own base, by adding a new Fixed-group convergence block to cascade.rs's solve_cascade — structurally mirroring the pre-existing Linked-group convergence block at lines 314-379 — that iterates input.groups.fixed.values(), computes one shared target via the existing fixed_group_target function, and assigns that target to every member of each Fixed group, participating in the same `while changed` fixpoint loop; (2) call the existing, fully-implemented pre_mutation_checks divergence/napi-drift detector from callisto-graph's real version-command orchestration path, before mutation, and actually consume its result (merge diagnostics, abort on divergence error); (3) add cross-group conflict detection to GroupTable::resolve so that two differently-spelled group members that resolve to the same PackageId across two different groups produce GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership instead of silently overwriting one group's claim with the other's, and deduplicate same-group duplicate spellings so a PackageId reachable under two spellings within one group appears exactly once in that group's resolved members.\n\n=== revision_note ===\nCorrected after canon-exit-gate retry 1 returned 7 blockers, all addressed: BLK-01 (critical) -- bug 1 was misdiagnosed as a fix to raise()'s per-sibling loop (cascade.rs:464-478), which the exit-gate proved unreachable for AC-001's seed-path scenario (solve_cascade computes seeded targets itself at line 198, before raise() ever runs) and, even when raise() does run, is guarded by `sev > sib_sev` which is false for AC-001's equal-severity siblings. Restructured scope, api_surface (replaced the 'cascade::raise' entry with a new 'cascade::solve_cascade (new Fixed-group convergence block)' entry describing a block mirroring the existing Linked-group block at lines 314-379), and AC-001/AC-002 to target a new Fixed-group convergence block inside solve_cascade's fixpoint loop instead, with AC-001's scenario now explicitly seeded (not raise()-triggered). Added two non_goals documenting that raise()'s existing loop is left unmodified (superseded, not removed) and that fixed_group_target's SemVer-only hardcoding is a known pre-existing gap out of scope for this track (BLK-05's second half). BLK-02 -- AC-004 was unobservable through plan_snapshot (which discards cascade targets); restated AC-004 to assert directly on run_cascade's CascadeOutcome.targets, with justification resting on structurally identical CascadeInput construction rather than a nonexistent observation path. BLK-03 -- AC-010c required an unstated resolve() behavior change forbidden by the original non_goals; added an explicit dedup requirement to the GroupTable::resolve api_surface entry (`.dedup()` after the existing `.sort()` calls at lines 164/195) and carved out an exception in non_goals item 4. BLK-04 -- fixed the fixed_group_target call sketch to the real five-argument signature (g, base, severities, tags, pre) in the new solve_cascade api_surface entry. BLK-05 -- AC-001 now states fully concrete fixture values (base_versions = {A: 2.0.0, B: 0.1.0}, tags.last_tag(A)=Some, tags.last_tag(B)=None, both seeded Minor -> both target 2.1.0) with the alignment-base mechanism (base[released[0]]) stated explicitly; added a non_goal covering the SemVer-only/PEP440 gap in fixed_group_target rather than leaving it ambiguous. BLK-06 -- AC-005 restated against the actual returned VersionPlan.bumps and SnapshotReport.bumps values instead of the unobservable private `snapshot_versions` local, and the unrunnable before/after framing was dropped. BLK-07 -- the plan_version api_surface entry now lists pre_mutation_checks's real six arguments (adding &ws.graph and ws.root) and corrects the tags borrow note (ws.tags() already returns &TagIndex, so `tags` is passed directly, not `&tags`).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a2979bd2-db1f-44a6-8e1c-6ad79197688f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:46:24.888Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== purpose ===\nWire three already-implemented but currently disconnected/broken pieces of callisto's fixed-group version engine into the real command call paths: (1) make fixed-group siblings converge on a single shared group-aligned target version instead of each bumping independently from its own base, by adding a new Fixed-group convergence block to cascade.rs's solve_cascade — structurally mirroring the pre-existing Linked-group convergence block at lines 314-379 — that iterates input.groups.fixed.values(), computes one shared target via the existing fixed_group_target function, and assigns that target to every member of each Fixed group, participating in the same `while changed` fixpoint loop; (2) call the existing, fully-implemented pre_mutation_checks divergence/napi-drift detector from callisto-graph's real version-command orchestration path, before mutation, and actually consume its result (merge diagnostics, abort on divergence error); (3) add cross-group conflict detection to GroupTable::resolve so that two differently-spelled group members that resolve to the same PackageId across two different groups produce GraphError::ConflictingGroupMembership instead of silently overwriting one group's claim with the other's, and deduplicate same-group duplicate spellings so a PackageId reachable under two spellings within one group appears exactly once in that group's resolved members.\n\n=== revision_note ===\nCorrected after canon-exit-gate retry 1 returned 7 blockers, all addressed: BLK-01 (critical) -- bug 1 was misdiagnosed as a fix to raise()'s per-sibling loop (cascade.rs:464-478), which the exit-gate proved unreachable for AC-001's seed-path scenario (solve_cascade computes seeded targets itself at line 198, before raise() ever runs) and, even when raise() does run, is guarded by `sev > sib_sev` which is false for AC-001's equal-severity siblings. Restructured scope, api_surface (replaced the 'cascade::raise' entry with a new 'cascade::solve_cascade (new Fixed-group convergence block)' entry describing a block mirroring the existing Linked-group block at lines 314-379), and AC-001/AC-002 to target a new Fixed-group convergence block inside solve_cascade's fixpoint loop instead, with AC-001's scenario now explicitly seeded (not raise()-triggered). Added two non_goals documenting that raise()'s existing loop is left unmodified (superseded, not removed) and that fixed_group_target's SemVer-only hardcoding is a known pre-existing gap out of scope for this track (BLK-05's second half). BLK-02 -- AC-004 was unobservable through plan_snapshot (which discards cascade targets); restated AC-004 to assert directly on run_cascade's CascadeOutcome.targets, with justification resting on structurally identical CascadeInput construction rather than a nonexistent observation path. BLK-03 -- AC-010c required an unstated resolve() behavior change forbidden by the original non_goals; added an explicit dedup requirement to the GroupTable::resolve api_surface entry (`.dedup()` after the existing `.sort()` calls at lines 164/195) and carved out an exception in non_goals item 4. BLK-04 -- fixed the fixed_group_target call sketch to the real five-argument signature (g, base, severities, tags, pre) in the new solve_cascade api_surface entry. BLK-05 -- AC-001 now states fully concrete fixture values (base_versions = {A: 2.0.0, B: 0.1.0}, tags.last_tag(A)=Some, tags.last_tag(B)=None, both seeded Minor -> both target 2.1.0) with the alignment-base mechanism (base[released[0]]) stated explicitly; added a non_goal covering the SemVer-only/PEP440 gap in fixed_group_target rather than leaving it ambiguous. BLK-06 -- AC-005 restated against the actual returned VersionPlan.bumps and SnapshotReport.bumps values instead of the unobservable private `snapshot_versions` local, and the unrunnable before/after framing was dropped. BLK-07 -- the plan_version api_surface entry now lists pre_mutation_checks's real six arguments (adding &ws.graph and ws.root) and corrects the tags borrow note (ws.tags() already returns &TagIndex, so `tags` is passed directly, not `&tags`).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3bcaf4a-417d-4e36-bd0e-ec2ac4704030","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
