etry-2 borrow fix only half landed.** All three sketches in the plan_version api_surface entry now read `&amp;ws.root`, but AC-009 — the normative criterion — still says pre_mutation_checks receives \"`&amp;ws.graph` and `ws.root`\". The parameter is `root: &amp;Path` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/groups.rs:18-25`) and `Workspace.root` is `pub root: PathBuf` behind `&amp;Workspace` (`crates/callisto-graph/src/lib.rs:54`), so `ws.root` is both a type mismatch and a move out of borrowed content. The spec now contradicts itself between its two layers. Fix: `&amp;ws.root` in AC-009 only; the bare occurrence in `revision_note` is historical narrative and needs no edit.\n\n**Confirmed clean** (so no rework is wasted there): purpose no longer mandates the retracted dedup; the retraction is documented in both revision_note and reasoning with no live `.dedup()`/AC-010c mandate anywhere; AC-003's thirteen literal line numbers are exact, there is no fourteenth construction site in the workspace, and I read every group construction feeding them — `cascade.rs:678,759` and `cascade_tests.rs:229,302` are `GroupKind::Linked`, the other nine are `GroupTable::default()`, so the `TagIndex::empty()` claim holds. Also re-verified against source: CascadeInput's 8 fields, the Linked block at 314-379, raise()'s loop at 464-478, bump_target's Pep440 dispatch at 398-401, fixed_group_target's five-arg signature and SemVer hardcoding at groups.rs:137, pre_mutation_checks's six-arg signature, resolve()'s unchecked inserts at 149/180, all three GraphError variants' field shapes, `#[from] ManifestError` making `NapiTargetsIndex::load(...)?` legal in plan_version, AC-007b's package.json path convention and error shapes, AC-014's premise that snapshot.rs never calls `ws.tags()` today, and AC-012's premise that `crates/callisto-graph/tests/config_resolve_tests.rs` exists with conflict-free fixtures.\n\nOne non-blocking note for whoever reviews: AC-011's clause \"ConflictingGroupMembership is not constructed anywhere during that resolve() call\" is not externally observable, but it is redundant with the criterion's testable `Ok(..)` assertion, so I did not raise it as a blocker.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>118372</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>37</tool_uses><duration_ms>762300</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
