**AC-009 borrow.** The criterion now reads `&amp;ws.root`, matching `root: &amp;Path` at `groups.rs:18-25` against `pub root: PathBuf` (`lib.rs:54`) behind `&amp;Workspace`. The one surviving bare `ws.root` is inside `revision_note`'s BLK-07 narration — historical prose, no normative force.\n\n### Independent re-verification (defect classes from prior rounds specifically hunted)\n\n- **Non-existent symbols** (round 3's class): every symbol, signature, and field name in the spec exists as cited — `ConflictingGroupMembership { package, groups }` at `error.rs:129`, `fixed_group_target`'s five args, `pre_mutation_checks`'s six, `NapiTargetsIndex::load`, `TagIndex::empty`, `ManifestError::Parse { path, format: PackageJson }`. All 15 line-number citations are exact.\n- **Borrow/compile errors** (round 2's class): borrow-checked every api_surface sketch. `ws.tags()` returns `&amp;TagIndex` so `tags` not `&amp;tags` is right; `&amp;PathBuf` deref-coerces at the call site; `NapiTargetsIndex::load`'s `ManifestError` propagates via `#[from]` at `error.rs:19`; the Fixed block's `&amp;out.severities` borrow ends at the owned `Version` before `out.targets.insert`.\n- **Unreachable mechanism** (round 1's class): traced AC-001's arithmetic through real code — seed pass yields A=2.1.0/B=0.2.0, the new block's `fixed_group_target` returns 2.1.0 from `base[released[0]]`, overwriting B. Critically, the inner worklist loop **reads** `out.targets[&amp;pkg]` (`cascade.rs:215`) rather than recomputing, so re-queuing B does not revert it and the fixpoint terminates on pass two. No oscillation. I also confirmed AC-010's fixture isn't pre-empted by `validate_syntactic` (`config/groups.rs:99-121`), which is keyed on raw member strings and scoped per-kind — both differently-spelled fixtures slip past it and reach `resolve()`.\n- AC-003's thirteen pre-existing literals: workspace-wide grep confirms the enumeration is complete, and I read every group feeding them — all Linked or `GroupTable::default()`, so `TagIndex::empty()` is uniformly valid. `TagIndex` is publicly re-exported (`lib.rs:31`, `lib.rs:50`), so the six external integration-test literals can name it.\n- AC-012 and AC-014 premises both hold (`tests/config_resolve_tests.rs` exists; `snapshot.rs` genuinely never calls `ws.tags()`, and `tags_laziness_test.rs` documents the deterministic CommandRunner-fallback technique).\n\n### Gate conditions\n\nAll four hold without relaxation: 15 criteria all assert concrete observables (exact versions, exact `Err` variants, exact build command); zero TBDs; five error criteria tagged `is_error_case: true` covering all three bugs; scope is one field + 15 call sites + one ~30-line mirrored block + ~20 lines of wiring.\n\nTwo non-blocking observations are recorded in `reasoning` rather than issued as blockers, since neither makes a criterion unverifiable: AC-011's \"not constructed anywhere\" clause is unobservable but redundant with its testable `Ok(..)` assertion, and AC-008 doesn't pin strict-mode behavior (`escalate()` is a no-op under default `VersionOptions`).\n\n`retry_count` is 4, past the escalation threshold — but the escalation rule substitutes for issuing *another fail*. The spec meets every condition, so escalation does not apply. Cleared for `vector`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>112299</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>45</tool_uses><duration_ms>410406</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
