ked or `GroupTable::default()`, so `TagIndex::empty()` is uniformly valid. `TagIndex` is publicly re-exported (`lib.rs:31`, `lib.rs:50`), so the six external integration-test literals can name it.\n- AC-012 and AC-014 premises both hold (`tests/config_resolve_tests.rs` exists; `snapshot.rs` genuinely never calls `ws.tags()`, and `tags_laziness_test.rs` documents the deterministic CommandRunner-fallback technique).\n\n### Gate conditions\n\nAll four hold without relaxation: 15 criteria all assert concrete observables (exact versions, exact `Err` variants, exact build command); zero TBDs; five error criteria tagged `is_error_case: true` covering all three bugs; scope is one field + 15 call sites + one ~30-line mirrored block + ~20 lines of wiring.\n\nTwo non-blocking observations are recorded in `reasoning` rather than issued as blockers, since neither makes a criterion unverifiable: AC-011's \"not constructed anywhere\" clause is unobservable but redundant with its testable `Ok(..)` assertion, and AC-008 doesn't pin strict-mode behavior (`escalate()` is a no-op under default `VersionOptions`).\n\n`retry_count` is 4, past the escalation threshold — but the escalation rule substitutes for issuing *another fail*. The spec meets every condition, so escalation does not apply. Cleared for `vector`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>112299</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>45</tool_uses><duration_ms>410406</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"e5551b4d-1548-470b-8310-861ebbdff8a8","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:15:58.501Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
