{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:43:38.452Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae9f8a38e0301a543</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/ae9f8a38e0301a543.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Produce plan@1 for fixed-group cascade spec\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All 16 acceptance criteria are covered, no extras, JSON is valid against the plan@1 shape. The plan is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI produced a `plan@1` decomposing SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS into 12 sequenced tasks (T01–T12), grounded in a full read of the live source (not just the spec's api_surface claims) — every file path, line number, and signature the spec cited was independently re-verified against current code, and one path was corrected: `GroupTable::resolve` lives at `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs`, not `config/groups.rs` alone.\n\n**Task sequencing** (4 batches):\n- **B1 (T01–T04)**: Add `tags: &amp;TagIndex` to `CascadeInput` and update all 15 real/test construction sites (cascade.rs struct + 7 in-file test literals, cascade_tests.rs's 6 literals, version.rs's and snapshot.rs's real production sites). T04 closes with the full-crate compile check (AC-003) plus three new snapshot.rs tests pinning AC-005, AC-006, AC-014.\n- **B2 (T05)**: New Fixed-group convergence block in `solve_cascade`, proven via a single test that builds a *real* `TagIndex` (reusing tags.rs's own `FakeGitTagRunner`/`non_repo_dir` pattern) and calls `run_cascade` directly — satisfying AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, and AC-013's bug-1 clause in one shot.\n- **B3 (T06–T09)**: Wires `pre_mutation_checks` + `NapiTargetsIndex` into `plan_version`, tested exclusively through `plan_version` itself (never the helper directly) via real `Workspace::load` git fixtures — covers AC-007, AC-007b, AC-008, AC-009, AC-013's bug-2 clause.\n- **B4 (T10–T12)**: Cross-group conflict detection in `GroupTable::resolve` via a single `claimed_by` map shared across the fixed/linked loops, tested through real TOML-parsed `Workspace::load` fixtures (extending the existing `config_resolve_tests.rs` pattern) — covers AC-010, AC-010b, AC-011, AC-012, AC-013's bug-3 clause.\n\nEvery task has an exact failing-test-first step, exact implementation code, exact pass/fail commands, and a conventional commit message. All 16 acceptance criteria (AC-001–AC-013, AC-007b, AC-010b, AC-014) are covered — verified programmatically against `expected` set, zero missing/extra.\n\n**Output files**:\n- `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/plan-fixed-group-cascade.json` — the full plan@1 artifact\n\n**Spec provenance embedded in the plan**:\n- `spec_file_path`: `.claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json`\n- `spec_hash`: `sha256:5050ccacc14ab9b144a88e934dbadde003e480251a50227cc011a8b32249306e`\n- `linked_requirement`: `REQ-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>194677</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>1553159</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
