d cleanly.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"T01\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"Verified live code against spec api_surface (CascadeInput struct location, TagIndex::empty() signature, tags module path)\",\n    \"RED: confirmed baseline grep empty before field added\",\n    \"Added tags field + TagIndex import to CascadeInput only\",\n    \"RED: confirmed 7 missing-field errors in cascade.rs at expected lines\",\n    \"Added tags: &amp;TagIndex::empty() to all 7 test literals\",\n    \"GREEN: confirmed zero cascade.rs errors remain\",\n    \"Confirmed only T02/T03-scoped files (snapshot.rs, version.rs) still fail, as expected\",\n    \"cargo fmt -p callisto-graph (no changes needed)\",\n    \"Committed\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"bb9d3aaa4f66fbb19425b82a9e9de8077214d8a6\",\n  \"concerns\": null,\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [],\n  \"reasoning\": \"T01's covers_criteria is an empty array in the plan, so no spec acceptance criteria apply to this task -- it is pure struct-plumbing to unblock later tasks. No precision_tests were supplied. The 'test' proven red-then-green here is the compile-time exhaustiveness check on CascadeInput's 7 pre-existing literals in cascade.rs itself, exactly as the plan's steps specify.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>55111</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>267106</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
