{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T18:28:01.333Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a870687f19ae05fbe</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_016bTE8TU4TKnRsm46s2S5nC</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a870687f19ae05fbe.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Implement T03 (plan_version TagIndex binding)\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task complete. Summary:\n\n**T03** — Bind and pass a real TagIndex into `plan_version`'s CascadeInput\n\n- RED confirmed: `cargo check -p callisto-graph --lib --message-format=short 2&gt;&amp;1 | grep 'commands/version.rs'` produced `error[E0063]: missing field 'tags'` at line 70, exactly as the plan predicted.\n- Implementation (minimal, matches plan steps exactly):\n  - `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:28` — added `let tags = ws.tags()?;`\n  - `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:44` — changed `ws.tags()?,` to `tags,` in the `aggregate(...)` call\n  - `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs:79` — added `tags,` field to the `CascadeInput { ... }` literal\n- GREEN confirmed: same grep now returns empty — no errors attributable to `commands/version.rs`.\n- `cargo fmt -p callisto-graph` ran clean; `cargo clippy --all-targets` shows zero findings for `commands/version.rs` (the only remaining error is the pre-existing `missing field tags` in `crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs`, which is T04's scope, not mine, as expected).\n- `commands/version.rs` has no inline `#[cfg(test)]` module, so there's no unit test target to run separately; the crate-wide `cargo test --lib commands::version::` cannot fully link yet because T04 (snapshot.rs) hasn't landed — that failure is entirely attributable to `snapshot.rs`, confirmed by isolating it in clippy/test output.\n- Committed as `b718f61`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"T03\",\n  \"status\": \"done\",\n  \"steps_completed\": [\n    \"Read task T03 from plan\",\n    \"Confirmed covers_criteria is empty for T03 (no spec criteria reading required)\",\n    \"RED: ran cargo check, confirmed missing-field E0063 error at commands/version.rs:70\",\n    \"Added `let tags = ws.tags()?;` binding after base_versions\",\n    \"Replaced `ws.tags()?` with `tags` in aggregate() call\",\n    \"Added `tags,` field to CascadeInput literal\",\n    \"GREEN: ran cargo check, confirmed zero errors for commands/version.rs\",\n    \"Ran cargo fmt -p callisto-graph\",\n    \"Ran cargo clippy --all-targets, confirmed zero findings for commands/version.rs (remaining error isolated to out-of-scope snapshot.rs)\",\n    \"Committed scoped fix\"\n  ],\n  \"test_result\": \"pass\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"b718f61\",\n  \"criteria_evidence\": [],\n  \"concerns\": \"commands/version.rs has no inline unit tests, so 'its own tests pass' reduces to the cargo check compile-cleanliness verification specified by the plan's own RED/GREEN steps; full crate test suite (cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib) still fails to link due to T04 (commands/snapshot.rs) not yet landing a `tags` field on its own CascadeInput literal — confirmed via isolated grep that this failure is unrelated to my change.\"\n}\n```</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>47518</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>13</tool_uses><duration_ms>100354</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
