dings worth flagging now:**\n1. The mutation run is **not** dead as reported — cargo-mutants (PID 11538) is still actively running, correctly scoped to the four changed files. It's at 36/113. All 21 survivors so far are in `cascade_action`, `coverage`, and `caret_covers` — pre-existing untouched functions (`cascade_action` is explicitly Track 9's scope). It has not yet reached the new code.\n2. `GroupTable::from_groups` (`config/groups.rs:259-289`) is a **third** membership-building path with no conflict check of any kind. It's `pub` and re-exported, currently test-only. Not a spec violation (the spec scoped the fix to `resolve`), but a real sibling gap for the verdict.\n\nI'm holding the verdict until `cargo test -p callisto-graph` completes and I've run the workspace regression checks — I won't certify a pass on an unobserved test result. I'll report as soon as they land.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>105435</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>401034</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
