{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:43:29.053Z","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3b6b1774ff25dddd</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a3b6b1774ff25dddd.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Exit-gate Track 1 implementation\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both checks remain in flight — `cargo test` is heavily contended by the parallel `cargo-mutants` run consuming all cores. I have background waiters on both and will report the moment they resolve.\n\nSummary of where the verdict stands, pending those two results:\n\n**Earned so far (verified by reading code, not pointers):** AC-001, AC-002, AC-004, AC-006, AC-007, AC-007b, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-010b, AC-011, AC-012, AC-013, AC-014. AC-003 and \"all tests pass\" are blocked on the suite result.\n\n**Gaps that will appear in the verdict regardless of outcome:**\n1. **Mutation coverage incomplete** — the run is live and correctly scoped, but was not complete at gate time. Its status will be recorded, not assumed.\n2. **`GroupTable::from_groups` sibling gap** (`crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs:259-289`) — a third, public, membership-building path with no conflict check. Test-only today; not a spec violation, but it can construct a `GroupTable` that violates the invariant `resolve` now enforces.\n3. **`fixed_group_target`'s SemVer hardcoding is now newly reachable from production.** The spec explicitly non-goals it, but wiring the block in changes its blast radius: in `plan_version` a mixed-grammar group is caught by `pre_mutation_checks` first, but `plan_snapshot` deliberately does *not* call that check (AC-006), so a homogeneous all-PEP440 fixed group can now reach `SemVerVersioning.bump` and return `Err` — a new failure path in `plan_snapshot` that did not exist before. Accepted by the spec, but worth flagging downstream.\n4. **Semver-breaking public API change** — `CascadeInput` gained a required field and is re-exported from a publishable AGPL crate.\n\n**Two test-robustness nits (not blockers):** the AC-005 test asserts a version *prefix* rather than equality to a single shared version and has no non-emptiness guard (though `MissingGroupMember` on load makes it non-vacuous in practice); the AC-014 test asserts only `is_err()` without pinning the error variant, so an unrelated failure would satisfy it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>105075</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>756437</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
