tform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json', name: 'my-lib.linux-x64-gnu'), and a computed PlannedBump for the owner from version X to version Y, running commands::version::plan_version produces a VersionPlan whose platform_writes contains a PlatformWrite { manifest: 'platform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json', version: Y } entry -- the platform manifest's target version tracks its owner's bump target exactly, not an independently-computed version.\",\n    \"Given the same scenario, and the owner's own canonical manifest (e.g. a sibling package.json, if the owner ecosystem is npm/hybrid, or another workspace package) declares an optionalDependencies entry naming the platform package ('my-lib.linux-x64-gnu': '<old version>'), plan_version's VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates contains an OptionalDepUpdate entry for that manifest updating that dependency name to version Y.\",\n    \"Given a Fixed group with NO GroupMember::PlatformManifest members (the ordinary case), plan_version's platform_writes and optional_dep_updates remain empty Vecs -- no regression for workspaces without platform packages.\",\n    \"Given a Fixed group's owner package receiving NO version bump this run (e.g. no changeset, Severity::None), no PlatformWrite or OptionalDepUpdate entry is produced for that group's platform members -- platform-manifest writes are strictly driven by an actual owner bump, never speculative.\",\n    \"Fix 1 (dormant bug, apply_version_plan consumption side): active_ecosystems (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, currently derived only from plan.bumps) is extended to also derive ecosystem membership from plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates' manifest paths, so that when opts.refresh_lockfiles is true and a plan contains only platform_writes/optional_dep_updates entries (no bumps), the correct ecosystem's lockfile (e.g. package-lock.json/pnpm-lock.yaml for an npm platform manifest) is both refreshed and staged, exactly as it already is for an ordinary plan.bumps-only plan.\",\n    \"Fix 1 regression: given an ordinary plan with only plan.bumps entries (no platform_writes/optional_dep_updates), active_ecosystems and lockfile refresh/staging behavior is byte-for-byte unchanged from before this fix -- all existing apply.rs tests pass unmodified.\",\n    \"Fix 2 (dormant bug, apply_version_plan consumption side): the platform_writes dispatch loop in apply_version_plan gains a precondition check mirroring the existing bump loops' current==expected pattern: PlatformWrite gains a `from: Version` field (the plan-time-observed current version of the platform manifest), and the loop errors with GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion (the same variant the sibling bump loops already use) if the platform manifest's actual on-disk current version does not match `from` at apply time, instead of silently overwriting it with `version` unconditionally.\",\n    \"Fix 2 regression: given a platform manifest whose on-disk version exactly matches the plan's PlatformWrite.from at apply time (the ordinary, non-drifted case), apply_version_plan succeeds and writes `version` exactly as before -- no behavior change for the non-drifted path.\",\n    \"Every acceptance criterion is proven through the real, live call path (commands::version::plan_version for the planning-logic criteria; crate::apply::apply_version_plan for the two consumption-side fixes), not just isolated unit tests of a helper function called directly.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"commands::snapshot::plan_snapshot and commands::pr_body's own platform_writes/optional_dep_updates population -- separate command entry points, explicitly deferred; this track covers plan_version only (state the reason: snapshot mode's synthetic versioning and pr_body's preview-only nature don't need real platform-manifest writes the way a real version-and-apply run does -- but the drafter should confirm this reasoning is sound and state it explicitly, not assume it).\",\n    \"Building a NEW planning-logic path for optionalDependencies updates unrelated to platform packages (e.g. an ordinary cross-package optionalDependencies bump with no napi/platform-manifest involvement) -- OptionalDepUpdate's only production source in this track is the platform-package-tracks-its-owner case.\",\n    \"Any change to the Manifest trait, ManifestFormat::from_path, or update_optional_dependencies's own internal logic -- both already exist and are correct, this track only adds a new call-site producer.\",\n    \"Redesigning apply_version_plan's write-batching (Spec A/Spec B's classify_manifest_writes) to fold platform_writes/optional_dep_updates into the batched-write groups -- the two dispatch loops remain structurally separate, sequential loops; this track only adds the missing precondition check and lockfile-ecosystem awareness to them, not a batching redesign.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n# Background context for grounding (verify against live code yourself, do not trust this paraphrase)\n\n`GroupMember::PlatformManifest { owner: PackageId, role: ManifestRole, path: PathBuf, name: String }` is defined in `crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs`. `PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf, version: Version }` and `OptionalDepUpdate { manifest: PathBuf, updates: Vec<(String, Version)> }` are defined in `crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs`. `commands/version.rs`'s `plan_version` (just modified by Track 1, now also calling `pre_mutation_checks` and constructing a `NapiTargetsIndex` before `run_cascade`) hardcodes both fields to `Vec::new()` in its final `VersionPlan` construction. `crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs`'s `apply_version_plan` already has two dispatch loops consuming these fields (landed in a separate, already-committed change with only one happy-path test) — read that code directly to confirm the two dormant-bug claims above before writing acceptance criteria referencing them. `active_ecosystems` and the lockfile refresh/staging logic are also in `apply.rs` — read the actual current derivation before writing Fix 1's acceptance criteria. `GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion` is an existing error variant used by the sibling bump loops — confirm its exact field shape before referencing it in Fix 2's criteria.\n\nThis is \"Track 2\" of a larger, already-approved 12-track remediation plan. Track 1 (fixed-group cascade correctness) just shipped — this track depends on Track 1's group-aligned target computation (a platform package's owner's bump target must be the CORRECT group-aligned version, not the old per-sibling-independent-bump version, or this track would silently propagate the same divergence bug into platform manifests). This repo's established process (`.claude/plans/ACTIVE.md`): full canon→vector→lambda pipeline for a track like this. `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` hard workspace invariant. `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` mandatory CI. Verify every code-location/line-number/field-shape claim above against the live code before trusting it — this session's Track 1 spec went through 4 exit-gate rounds specifically because early drafts contained small inaccuracies about the actual code.\n\nProduce a spec@1 with purpose, scope, non_goals (at least the four out_of_scope items above, stated as non_goals, with the reasoning for the snapshot.rs/pr_body.rs deferral made explicit rather than assumed), acceptance_criteria (testable propositions, error cases marked is_error_case: true), and an api_surface section documenting any new/changed function signature or struct field (PlatformWrite gaining a `from` field is exactly such a change).","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2/tasks/a85c448457c3bed14.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28cf3e96-13dc-43ce-a350-c667e245d9a4","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d