ly plan.bumps entries has byte-for-byte unchanged active_ecosystems/lockfile behavior.\",\n    \"Fix 2: PlatformWrite gains a `from: Version` field; the dispatch loop errors with GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion if the platform manifest's actual on-disk version doesn't match `from`, instead of silently overwriting.\",\n    \"Fix 2 regression: a platform manifest whose on-disk version matches `from` writes successfully exactly as before.\",\n    \"Every criterion proven through the real, live call path (plan_version / apply_version_plan), not isolated unit tests of a helper called directly.\"\n  ],\n  \"out_of_scope\": [\n    \"plan_snapshot and pr_body's own platform_writes/optional_dep_updates population -- deferred, reasoning to be confirmed against live code and stated explicitly.\",\n    \"A new planning-logic path for optionalDependencies updates unrelated to platform packages.\",\n    \"Any change to the Manifest trait, ManifestFormat::from_path, or update_optional_dependencies's own internal logic.\",\n    \"Redesigning apply_version_plan's write-batching to fold these two fields into the batched-write groups.\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nRead the full spec@1 JSON from disk for complete acceptance criteria text. Note the drafter's own report says it found the requirement's pr_body.rs framing was imprecise (pr_body.rs calls plan_version directly, has no separate producer to defer) and corrected this in the spec's non_goals/scope -- verify this correction is handled sensibly and doesn't leave a gap. Also note AC-007 (multi-target-per-owner cardinality) was added by the drafter beyond what the requirement's done_when literally enumerated -- assess whether this is a reasonable, well-grounded addition (a realistic napi-rs scenario) or unsupported scope expansion. Output a structured evidence report with supported, unsupported, and overfitted arrays plus a reasoning scratchpad.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e