{"parentUuid":"ace21c77-69e1-468e-81ec-a64e969b5063","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce8zDYv2u3m9cHXtDXxwx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014kBibEphz99jmWtULGR8Mf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Audit Track 2 spec quality","subagent_type":"canon:auditor","prompt":"Adversarially audit the spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track2-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES, callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto — builds the planning logic to populate VersionPlan.platform_writes/optional_dep_updates from Fixed-group GroupMember::PlatformManifest members, plus fixes two dormant bugs in apply_version_plan's already-landed consumption side).\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk. This spec just went through canon-verifier, which found: 10 of 14 criteria trace directly to the source requirement; 4 (AC-002, AC-004, AC-007, AC-008) were drafter-added without direct requirement citation but are plausible completeness additions (AC-002: how PlatformWrite.from is populated at plan time; AC-004: the negative case of AC-003 — no matching optionalDependencies entry means no speculative creation; AC-007: multi-platform-target-per-owner cardinality, a realistic napi-rs scenario; AC-008: error case for a missing/malformed platform manifest file). One internal cross-reference bug was found and already fixed (non_goals referenced \"AC-011\" where \"AC-008\" was meant). Your job: judge whether these 4 additions are legitimate, necessary completeness (matching your own \"missing error cases\" audit dimension) or should be trimmed/flagged, and do your own independent five-dimension pass.\n\nCheck the standard five dimensions: untestable/vague acceptance criteria, ambiguous phrasing admitting two valid interpretations, missing error cases for nil/malformed/out-of-range inputs, scope overlap with other workspace specs (.claude/specs/ directory — particularly SPEC-TRACK1-FIXED-GROUP-CASCADE-CORRECTNESS.json, track-b-idempotent-apply.json, SPEC-APPLY-BATCH-002.json, all of which touch adjacent-but-distinct areas of apply.rs/cascade.rs — confirm no real overlap, especially given this spec's Fix 1/Fix 2 both touch apply.rs which SPEC-APPLY-BATCH-002's classify_manifest_writes also touches), and TBDs/incomplete sections. Pay special attention to whether AC-002's derivation mechanism for PlatformWrite.from (reading the platform manifest's own current_version at plan time) is precisely specified enough that two competent implementers would produce the same code, since this is exactly the kind of underspecified-mechanism gap that caused Track 1's first exit-gate failure.\n\nFor every issue found, produce a specific rewritten suggested_fix. Output the standard JSON object with issues array and overall pass/fail verdict."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":566351,"output_tokens":1116,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1116,"cache_read_input_tokens":566351,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8zDW39U5TquTFe29yBZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"fa0df329-232a-4841-8bc7-5de7abf6e747","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:55:37.639Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d