{"parentUuid":"685f4209-2da3-4377-a3fc-6819f2ce2095","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"a324e89f-0d64-49f6-9a03-6612dd5892ad","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TxJLCDsP5P7kv9cWRGVetU","type":"tool_result","content":"--- PlatformWrite ---\nAdds a `from: Version` field (previously only `manifest` and `version` existed, crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs lines 45-49) capturing the platform manifest's on-disk version as observed by plan_version at plan time. Consumed by apply_version_plan's platform_writes dispatch loop as the expected-current-version precondition, mirroring PlannedBump.from's role in the sibling bump loops. This is a breaking change to any code constructing PlatformWrite directly (existing test fixtures in apply.rs a\n\n--- commands::version::plan_version ---\nSignature unchanged. Behavior changes: the returned VersionPlan.platform_writes and VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates are now populated per AC-001 through AC-008 (including AC-007b) instead of being hardcoded to Vec::new() (previously at commands/version.rs lines 262-263). Can now return a new error path (AC-008) when a Fixed group's platform manifest cannot be opened or read.\n\n--- apply::apply_version_plan ---\nSignature unchanged. Behavior changes: (1) active_ecosystems (apply.rs lines 325-349) is now also derived from plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates manifest paths, affecting which lockfiles get refreshed/staged (AC-009, AC-010, AC-011); (2) the platform_writes dispatch loop (apply.rs lines 244-252) gains a current-version precondition check against PlatformWrite.from before writing, returning GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion on mismatch instead of overwriting unconditionally,","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6b25806c-487e-48c9-899e-c3c280f3e58c","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:00:02.558Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"--- PlatformWrite ---\nAdds a `from: Version` field (previously only `manifest` and `version` existed, crates/callisto-graph/src/