why_it_survived\":\"no test distinguishes CatalogSpecNotRewritten from RangeNotRoundTrippable\"},\n    {\"id\":\"cascade.rs:299:31\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\"line\":299,\"mutation_description\":\"replace &gt; with &gt;= in raise-on-severity-increase guard\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no idempotency test at equal severity\"},\n    {\"id\":\"cascade.rs:333:24/336:32\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\"line\":333,\"mutation_description\":\"replace &gt; with &gt;= in Linked-group max_sev&gt;None / max_sev&gt;cur_sev guards\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no all-None-severity linked-group test\"},\n    {\"id\":\"cascade.rs:404:24/407:32 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\"line\":404,\"mutation_description\":\"replace &gt; with &gt;=/==/&lt; in Fixed-group convergence guards (mirrors 333/336, the new PLAN-TRACK1 block)\",\"why_it_survived\":\"same idempotency gap, on the newly-added Fixed-group code path\"},\n    {\"id\":\"cascade.rs:520:16 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\"line\":520,\"mutation_description\":\"replace &gt; with ==/&lt;/&gt;= in raise()\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no boundary test on raise()'s comparison\"},\n    {\"id\":\"cascade.rs:538 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\"line\":538,\"mutation_description\":\"replace * with +/- in convergence_bound(4*n+1)\",\"why_it_survived\":\"convergence_bound has no direct unit test at all\"},\n    {\"id\":\"cascade.rs:573 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs\",\"line\":573,\"mutation_description\":\"mutate guard/! /== in rewrite_spec\",\"why_it_survived\":\"rewrite_spec's guard branch untested for this condition\"},\n    {\"id\":\"snapshot.rs:88:26 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs\",\"line\":88,\"mutation_description\":\"replace == with != on ManifestRole::Canonical check\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no snapshot test with a non-Canonical manifest role present\"},\n    {\"id\":\"snapshot.rs:121:17 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs\",\"line\":121,\"mutation_description\":\"delete match arm RewriteOutcome::Rewritten(new_spec) in plan_snapshot\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no snapshot test distinguishes Rewritten vs LeftAlone/other outcome\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:57:21 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":57,\"mutation_description\":\"replace == with != on ver.is_prerelease() guard (PreMode::Exit synthesis)\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no test with a mixed stable+prerelease base_versions set under Exit mode\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:103:16 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":103,\"mutation_description\":\"replace == with != on sev==Severity::None skip guard\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no test with a mix of zero and non-zero severities in one outcome\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:130:26 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":130,\"mutation_description\":\"replace == with != on ManifestRole::Canonical check\",\"why_it_survived\":\"same class as snapshot.rs:88\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:156/160/164/174 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":156,\"mutation_description\":\"delete match arms for BumpReason::{FixedGroupUnion,LinkedGroupUnion,Cascade,PeerEscalation} in ChangeSource synthesis\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no test asserts the synthesized ChangeSource for any non-changeset-driven BumpReason\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:218/219 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":218,\"mutation_description\":\"replace &amp;&amp; with ||, delete ! in EmptyChangeset diagnostic gate\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no test isolates each of the three boolean components (consumed empty, opts.allow_empty_changesets, config.validation.allow_empty_changesets)\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:235:23 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":235,\"mutation_description\":\"replace == with != on state.mode==PreMode::Exit\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no test on pre_state_update/delete_pre_json for the non-Exit branch alongside Exit\"},\n    {\"id\":\"version.rs:248:24 (timeout)\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\"line\":248,\"mutation_description\":\"delete ! in seen.contains(&amp;stem) dedup guard\",\"why_it_survived\":\"no test replays an already-consumed changeset stem to check it isn't pushed twice\"},\n    {\"id\":\"groups.rs:71:9\",\"file\":\"crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs\",\"line\":71,\"mutation_description\":\"replace GroupTable::validate_syntactic body with Ok(())\",\"why_it_survived\":\"validate_syntactic is called live from config/resolve.rs:365 but no test ever supplies a duplicate group name, empty-members group, or intra-table conflicting member to trigger DuplicateGroupName/EmptyGroup/ConflictingGroupNames\"}\n  ],\n  \"precision_tests\": [\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:43:9\",\"test_name\":\"cascade_action_matrix_all_kind_coverage_pairs\",\"test_description\":\"Table-driven test over every (DepKind, Coverage) pair (Runtime/Optional/Build/Peer/Dev x Covers/DoesNotCover/Unknown) with peer_escalation both true and false, asserting exact CascadeDecision{severity,rewrite,governed_by,escalated}\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(cascade_action(Runtime, Covers, ...), CascadeDecision{severity:None,rewrite:false,governed_by:None,escalated:false,unknown_coverage:false})\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:49:9\",\"test_name\":\"cascade_action_matrix_all_kind_coverage_pairs\",\"test_description\":\"same table covers Peer/Covers row\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(cascade_action(Peer, Covers, ...).severity, Severity::None)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:55:9\",\"test_name\":\"cascade_action_peer_no_escalation_bumps_via_bump_severity\",\"test_description\":\"Peer + DoesNotCover with cfg.peer_escalation=false must fall through to the bump_severity arm, not the escalation arm\",\"assertion\":\"let d = cascade_action(Peer, DoesNotCover, Severity::None, &amp;cfg_no_escalation); assert!(!d.escalated); assert_eq!(d.governed_by, Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_BUMP_SEVERITY))\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:60:9\",\"test_name\":\"cascade_action_dev_dep_never_bumps\",\"test_description\":\"Dev dep kind must always yield Severity::None regardless of coverage\",\"assertion\":\"for cov in [Covers, DoesNotCover, Unknown] { assert_eq!(cascade_action(Dev, cov, Severity::Major, &amp;cfg).severity, Severity::None); }\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:50:33\",\"test_name\":\"cascade_action_peer_escalation_guard_both_conditions_required\",\"test_description\":\"peer_escalation=false with DoesNotCover must NOT escalate even though coverage condition is true\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(!cascade_action(Peer, DoesNotCover, sev, &amp;cfg_no_escalation).escalated)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:65:55(true)\",\"test_name\":\"cascade_action_always_mode_governed_by_only_when_severity_nonzero\",\"test_description\":\"CascadeMode::Always with Covers/Unknown and a resulting non-None severity sets governed_by=CASCADE_MODE; when severity resolves to None it must not\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(cascade_action(Runtime, Unknown, sev, &amp;cfg_always).governed_by, Some(ConfigKey::CASCADE_MODE)) for the non-None case, and assert_ne!(..., Some(CASCADE_MODE)) for a None-severity case\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:83:18\",\"test_name\":\"coverage_depspec_exact_equal_and_unequal\",\"test_description\":\"Direct unit test of coverage() for DepSpec::Exact with equal and unequal version\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(coverage(&amp;DepSpec::Exact(v.clone()), &amp;v).unwrap(), Coverage::Covers); assert_eq!(coverage(&amp;DepSpec::Exact(v), &amp;other).unwrap(), Coverage::DoesNotCover)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:126:16\",\"test_name\":\"caret_covers_boundary_equal_version\",\"test_description\":\"caret_covers(cur, cur) must be true (equal versions), and caret_covers(cur, older) must be false\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(caret_covers(&amp;v, &amp;v).unwrap()); assert!(!caret_covers(&amp;v_1_2_3, &amp;v_1_2_2).unwrap())\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:128:23(==)\",\"test_name\":\"caret_covers_major_zero_boundary\",\"test_description\":\"Distinguish cur_maj==0 (falls to minor-branch) from cur_maj&gt;0 (major-branch) explicitly: 0.5.0 vs 1.5.0 as cur\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(caret_covers(&amp;Version::semver(0,5,0), &amp;Version::semver(0,5,3)).unwrap()); assert!(!caret_covers(&amp;Version::semver(0,5,0), &amp;Version::semver(0,6,0)).unwrap())\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:129:25\",\"test_name\":\"caret_covers_major_branch_requires_major_match_only\",\"test_description\":\"cur_maj&gt;0: new_maj must match; new_min is irrelevant to coverage in this branch\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(caret_covers(&amp;Version::semver(1,2,0), &amp;Version::semver(1,9,0)).unwrap()); assert!(!caret_covers(&amp;Version::semver(1,2,0), &amp;Version::semver(2,0,0)).unwrap())\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:131:16\",\"test_name\":\"caret_covers_zero_zero_requires_exact_match\",\"test_description\":\"cur_maj==0 &amp;&amp; cur_min==0 (e.g. 0.0.3): only an exact version match is covered\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(caret_covers(&amp;Version::semver(0,0,3), &amp;Version::semver(0,0,3)).unwrap()); assert!(!caret_covers(&amp;Version::semver(0,0,3), &amp;Version::semver(0,0,4)).unwrap())\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:195:9\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_preserves_preexisting_reasons\",\"test_description\":\"Seed input.reasons with an entry for a package NOT touched by this cascade run and assert it survives unchanged in the outcome\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(outcome.reasons.get(&amp;untouched_pkg), Some(&amp;original_reason))\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:213:24\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_reports_accurate_iteration_count\",\"test_description\":\"Run a small deterministic cascade and assert CascadeOutcome.iterations equals the known expected pop count (not 0)\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(outcome.iterations, expected_count); assert!(outcome.iterations &gt; 0)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:233:39\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_opaque_spec_suppresses_unknown_coverage_diagnostic\",\"test_description\":\"Edge with DepSpec::Opaque and unknown coverage must NOT produce a diagnostic; a non-Opaque spec with unknown coverage must\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(outcome_opaque.diagnostics.is_empty()); assert!(!outcome_range.diagnostics.is_empty())\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:235:25\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_catalog_spec_gets_catalog_diagnostic_code\",\"test_description\":\"Edge with DepSpec::Catalog and unknown coverage must emit DiagnosticCode::CatalogSpecNotRewritten, not RangeNotRoundTrippable\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(outcome.diagnostics[0].code, DiagnosticCode::CatalogSpecNotRewritten)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:299:31\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_raise_is_idempotent_at_equal_severity\",\"test_description\":\"When a dependent's computed severity equals its current severity, raise() must not fire again / re-enqueue\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(worklist_len_before_second_pass, worklist_len_after)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:333:24/336:32\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_linked_group_none_severity_noop\",\"test_description\":\"Linked group where every member's severity is Severity::None must not enter the union block or mutate severities/targets\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(outcome.severities, input.seed.clone()) for an all-None-severity linked group\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:404:24/407:32 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"solve_cascade_fixed_group_none_severity_noop\",\"test_description\":\"Fixed group where every member's severity is Severity::None must not enter the Fixed-group convergence block (mirrors the Linked-group idempotency test on the new PLAN-TRACK1 code)\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(outcome.severities, input.seed.clone()) for an all-None-severity fixed group; assert outcome.targets unaffected\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"cascade.rs:538 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"convergence_bound_formula_direct\",\"test_description\":\"Direct unit test of convergence_bound(n) = 4n+1 for several n\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(convergence_bound(0), 1); assert_eq!(convergence_bound(3), 13); assert_eq!(convergence_bound(10), 41)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"snapshot.rs:88:26 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_snapshot_only_canonical_manifests_get_write_target\",\"test_description\":\"Package with both a Canonical and a non-Canonical manifest role: only the Canonical one appears in writes\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(writes.len(), 1); assert!(matches!(writes[0], VersionWriteTarget::Manifest(p) if p == canonical_path))\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"snapshot.rs:121:17 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_snapshot_rewritten_outcome_uses_new_spec_not_exact_fallback\",\"test_description\":\"A rewrite whose rewrite_spec() returns Rewritten(new_spec) must set rewrite.to = new_spec, distinct from the Exact(snap_to) fallback used for other outcomes\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(rewrite.to, new_spec); assert_ne!(rewrite.to, DepSpec::Exact(snap_to.clone()))\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"version.rs:57:21 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_version_exit_mode_only_synthesizes_for_prerelease_bases\",\"test_description\":\"PreMode::Exit with a mix of one prerelease and one stable base version: only the prerelease package gets synthesized Patch severity/PreRelease reason\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(agg.severities.contains_key(&amp;prerelease_pkg)); assert!(!agg.severities.contains_key(&amp;stable_pkg) || pre-existing entry unchanged)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"version.rs:103:16 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_version_skips_none_severity_packages_from_bumps\",\"test_description\":\"outcome.severities containing both a None and a non-None entry: only the non-None package appears in bumps\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(bumps.len(), 1); assert_eq!(bumps[0].package, non_none_pkg)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"version.rs:156/160/164/174 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_version_changesource_matches_bump_reason_variant\",\"test_description\":\"Four cases, one per BumpReason variant (FixedGroupUnion, LinkedGroupUnion, Cascade, PeerEscalation) with no changeset backing the bump: assert the synthesized ChangeSource in changelog_writes matches exactly\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(matches!(entry.source, ChangeSource::GroupUnion{kind: GroupKind::Fixed, ..})) and analogous assertions for the other three variants\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"version.rs:218/219 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_version_empty_changeset_diagnostic_gate_components\",\"test_description\":\"Three separate cases: (a) consumed empty + both flags false -&gt; diagnostic present; (b) consumed empty + opts.allow_empty_changesets=true -&gt; no diagnostic; (c) consumed empty + config.validation.allow_empty_changesets=true -&gt; no diagnostic\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(diagnostics.iter().any(|d| d.code==EmptyChangeset)) for (a); assert!(!diagnostics.iter().any(...)) for (b) and (c)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"version.rs:248:24 (timeout)\",\"test_name\":\"plan_version_pre_state_dedupes_already_seen_changeset_stems\",\"test_description\":\"A consumed changeset whose stem is already present in state.changesets must not be pushed a second time\",\"assertion\":\"assert_eq!(state.changesets.iter().filter(|s| **s == stem).count(), 1)\"},\n    {\"for_mutant_id\":\"groups.rs:71:9\",\"test_name\":\"validate_syntactic_rejects_duplicate_empty_and_conflicting_groups\",\"test_description\":\"Three cases against GroupTable::validate_syntactic directly: (a) two fixed groups sharing a name -&gt; DuplicateGroupName; (b) a group with an empty members list -&gt; EmptyGroup; (c) the same member name in two different fixed groups -&gt; ConflictingGroupNames\",\"assertion\":\"assert!(matches!(validate_syntactic(&amp;raw_dup).unwrap_err(), ConfigError::DuplicateGroupName{..})); assert!(matches!(validate_syntactic(&amp;raw_empty).unwrap_err(), ConfigError::EmptyGroup{..})); assert!(matches!(validate_syntactic(&amp;raw_conflict).unwrap_err(), ConfigError::ConflictingGroupNames{..}))\"}\n  ],\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"cargo-mutants ran cleanly (baseline built, 105 mutants generated, scoped correctly to the four target files) and I read the actual outcomes.json/missed.txt/timeout.txt, not just a summary. 28 mutants were unambiguously missed and 28 more timed out without any clear kill signal, against 41 caught. The pattern is structural, not incidental: cascade_action, caret_covers, and coverage() in cascade.rs — core decision logic for the Track 1 feature — have no direct unit tests at all, only indirect exercise through a handful of high-level solve_cascade integration tests that don't hit every branch/boundary. The brand-new PLAN-TRACK1 Fixed-group convergence block (cascade.rs ~383-420) mirrors the Linked-group block's untested idempotency guards. GroupTable::validate_syntactic — live-wired from config/resolve.rs:365 and directly implementing the cross-group conflict detection this track was about — has literally zero test coverage of any of its three error paths; deleting its entire body and returning Ok(()) unconditionally does not fail a single test. This is exactly the coverage-without-assertion failure mode: tests execute these code paths (via higher-level flows) but never pin down what should happen on the branches that matter. 25 precision tests are specified above, each targeting a distinct code path/boundary and referencing the exact mutant id(s) it kills.\"\n}\n```\n\n**Files relevant to this report:**\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/mutants.out/missed.txt`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/mutants.out/timeout.txt`, `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/mutants.out/outcomes.json`\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/cascade.rs` (primary gap: `cascade_action` lines 24-72, `coverage` lines 76-91, `caret_covers` lines 108-133, iteration/idempotency guards lines 213-407, `convergence_bound` line 537)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs` (lines 55-63, 100-104, 150-186, 216-219, 235, 248)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/snapshot.rs` (lines 87-90, 118-127)\n- `/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/crates/callisto-graph/src/config/groups.rs` (`validate_syntactic`, lines 70-131 — zero test coverage of any error branch)\n\nVerdict is **fail**. Per protocol, these 25 precision tests should go back to implementer as a targeted TDD cycle before the exit gate runs.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>77968</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>31</tool_uses><duration_ms>2194705</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"44aa6066-b200-4dc0-87be-5060f368994b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:04:12.150Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
