{"parentUuid":"012b56f6-39d0-47a9-b63d-37baa308ccee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce91BBPY9UYMCBEvQxKu2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dk4yYYWE1LpdVCHfPVab99","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track2-draft.json') as f:\n    d = json.load(f)\nfor c in d['acceptance_criteria']:\n    if c['id'] in ('AC-002','AC-005','AC-009','AC-010','AC-011'):\n        print('===', c['id'], '===')\n        print(c['criterion'])\n        print()\n\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2491,"cache_read_input_tokens":600359,"output_tokens":719,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":474},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":719,"cache_read_input_tokens":600359,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce91B6fGxVKNAn9MGMCpn","type":"assistant","uuid":"43feef01-f9e0-4641-b65a-f19e0e57276b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:08:09.336Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"43feef01-f9e0-4641-b65a-f19e0e57276b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6d6ce92c-c6ab-4d57-8252-f10d5d397707","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dk4yYYWE1LpdVCHfPVab99","type":"tool_result","content":"=== AC-002 ===\nIn the AC-001 scenario, PlatformWrite.from equals the version string currently declared in the platform manifest file at path P on disk at plan time. plan_version reads P via ManifestFormat::from_path(P) to detect format, then ManifestDecl::new(P, ManifestRole::Canonical, format) to open it and call current_version() -- ManifestRole::Canonical is used unconditionally for this read, regardless of the value of the owning GroupMember::PlatformManifest's own `role` field, so that a Cargo/TOML-formatted platform manifest (e.g. a maturin platform crate) opens successfully rather than tripping ManifestDecl::new's Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection (crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106). This mirrors the ManifestRole::Canonical construction already used by apply_version_plan's platform_writes and optional_dep_updates dispatch loops (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:247,257) when opening these same paths, so plan-time and apply-time reads of a given platform manifest use the same role and cannot diverge in how ManifestDecl validates it.\n\n=== AC-005 ===\nGiven a Fixed group with NO GroupMember::PlatformManifest members (only Package members), plan_version's VersionPlan.platform_writes and VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates are both empty Vecs for that group -- no regression for workspaces without platform packages.\n\n=== AC-009 ===\nFix 1 (apply.rs active_ecosystems): given a VersionPlan whose plan.bumps is empty but plan.platform_writes contains one entry pointing at an npm-ecosystem manifest path (e.g. 'platform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json'), and ApplyOptions.refresh_lockfiles == true and opts.transient == false, calling apply_version_plan causes the npm lockfile (package-lock.json or pnpm-lock.yaml, matching the detected npm workspace kind) to be refreshed and staged in modified_paths, exactly as it already is for an ordinary plan.bumps-only plan touching an npm manifest.\n\n=== AC-010 ===\nFix 1 (apply.rs active_ecosystems): given the AC-009 scenario but using plan.optional_dep_updates instead of plan.platform_writes (plan.bumps empty, one OptionalDepUpdate entry pointing at an npm-ecosystem manifest path, refresh_lockfiles == true, transient == false), calling apply_version_plan causes the npm lockfile to be refreshed and staged, matching AC-009's behavior for platform_writes.\n\n=== AC-011 ===\nFix 1 regression: given an ordinary VersionPlan with only plan.bumps entries populated (plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates both empty, as in every plan before this track), calling apply_version_plan with refresh_lockfiles == true produces byte-for-byte the same active_ecosystems set, the same lockfile refresh_results, and the same staged modified_paths as before this track's change -- confirmed by all pre-existing apply.rs tests passing unmodified.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"323e0341-2f16-4bfb-8b8c-3097c89a113b","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:08:11.568Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== AC-002 ===\nIn the AC-001 scenario, PlatformWrite.from equals the version string currently declared in the platform manifest file at path P on disk at plan time. plan_version reads P via ManifestFormat::from_path(P) to detect format, then ManifestDecl::new(P, ManifestRole::Canonical, format) to open it and call current_version() -- ManifestRole::Canonical is used unconditionally for this read, regardless of the value of the owning GroupMember::PlatformManifest's own `role` field, so that a Cargo/TOML-formatted platform manifest (e.g. a maturin platform crate) opens successfully rather than tripping ManifestDecl::new's Platform-role-vs-CargoToml-format rejection (crates/callisto-model/src/package.rs:104-106). This mirrors the ManifestRole::Canonical construction already used by apply_version_plan's platform_writes and optional_dep_updates dispatch loops (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:247,257) when opening these same paths, so plan-time and apply-time reads of a given platform manifest use the same role and cannot diverge in how ManifestDecl validates it.\n\n=== AC-005 ===\nGiven a Fixed group with NO GroupMember::PlatformManifest members (only Package members), plan_version's VersionPlan.platform_writes and VersionPlan.optional_dep_updates are both empty Vecs for that group -- no regression for workspaces without platform packages.\n\n=== AC-009 ===\nFix 1 (apply.rs active_ecosystems): given a VersionPlan whose plan.bumps is empty but plan.platform_writes contains one entry pointing at an npm-ecosystem manifest path (e.g. 'platform/my-lib.linux-x64-gnu/package.json'), and ApplyOptions.refresh_lockfiles == true and opts.transient == false, calling apply_version_plan causes the npm lockfile (package-lock.json or pnpm-lock.yaml, matching the detected npm workspace kind) to be refreshed and staged in modified_paths, exactly as it already is for an ordinary plan.bumps-only plan touching an npm manifest.\n\n=== AC-010 ===\nFix 1 (apply.rs active_ecosystems): given the AC-009 scenario but using plan.optional_dep_updates instead of plan.platform_writes (plan.bumps empty, one OptionalDepUpdate entry pointing at an npm-ecosystem manifest path, refresh_lockfiles == true, transient == false), calling apply_version_plan causes the npm lockfile to be refreshed and staged, matching AC-009's behavior for platform_writes.\n\n=== AC-011 ===\nFix 1 regression: given an ordinary VersionPlan with only plan.bumps entries populated (plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates both empty, as in every plan before this track), calling apply_version_plan with refresh_lockfiles == true produces byte-for-byte the same active_ecosystems set, the same lockfile refresh_results, and the same staged modified_paths as before this track's change -- confirmed by all pre-existing apply.rs tests passing unmodified.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43feef01-f9e0-4641-b65a-f19e0e57276b","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
