{"parentUuid":"0c9aa853-d8ac-4515-9d04-36e1e3799392","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce91GPp3hkKfnkJBgkSjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AduKTeU2D8pLXgNqv9iib8","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Exit-gate Track 2 spec (retry 2)","subagent_type":"canon:exit-gate","prompt":"Issue a binding pass/fail verdict on the spec@1 at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-callisto/ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118/scratchpad/spec-track2-draft.json (id SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES, callisto Rust monorepo at /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto). This is retry_count 2 — your prior pass (retry_count 1) failed with 4 blockers, all just fixed via direct, targeted edits:\n\n1. AC-009/AC-010 previously claimed npm lockfiles get \"refreshed AND staged\" — but apply_version_plan (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:353-407) has no npm refresh subprocess at all, only Cargo (`cargo update`) and Pypi (`uv lock`/`poetry lock`). Rewrote both to assert STAGING only (ApplyOutcome.staged includes the npm lockfile present on disk, matching apply.rs:411-421's unfiltered-by-workspace-kind staging table) and explicitly assert NO npm entry appears in ApplyOutcome.lockfile_refresh_results, matching the pre-existing behavior for any plan (npm never got refreshed before this track either).\n2. AC-002 named ManifestDecl::new but not the actual opener (callisto_manifests::open) or its required OpenContext, leaving the workspace-inherited-version Cargo case (a maturin platform crate with `version.workspace = true`) undefined -- with cargo_workspace: None it would actually error via ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited, contradicting AC-002's \"opens successfully\" claim. Fixed AC-002 to name open() explicitly and specify that plan_version derives OpenContext using the exact same pattern apply_version_plan already uses (crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs:118-130: WorkspaceCargoResolver::load + inheritance() for cargo_workspace, detect_npm_workspace_kind for npm_workspace_kind, both from the real workspace root, never None). Added new AC-002b specifically proving the workspace-inherited-version case resolves correctly end-to-end with this derivation.\n3. AC-005 asserted \"empty for that group\" but VersionPlan carries no per-group partition (PlatformWrite/OptionalDepUpdate have no group attribution field) -- rewrote to assert workspace-wide emptiness when no Fixed group anywhere has platform members, with an explanatory parenthetical.\n4. AC-011 asserted on active_ecosystems, a function-local binding with no external visibility -- rewrote to assert on ApplyOutcome.lockfile_refresh_results and ApplyOutcome.staged (the actual public fields a test can observe), with an explanatory parenthetical.\n\nAlso updated the apply_version_plan api_surface entry to say \"staged\" not \"refreshed/staged\" with an explanatory clause about npm having no refresh subprocess, and updated plan_version's api_surface entry to include the new AC-002b reference.\n\nRead the full spec fresh from disk — do not trust this summary, verify these four fixes actually landed and are internally consistent, don't just trust that they did. Independently re-verify every api_surface/acceptance-criteria claim against the live code in crates/callisto-graph/src/{apply.rs,plan.rs,commands/version.rs,config/groups.rs,groups.rs,cargo.rs}, crates/callisto-model/src/{package.rs,error.rs}, and crates/callisto-manifests/src/lib.rs, exactly as your prior pass did (it caught 4 real, non-cosmetic defects, so this level of scrutiny is necessary, not excessive) -- pay special attention to whether AC-002b's inherited-version scenario genuinely resolves correctly with the specified OpenContext derivation, and whether AC-009/AC-010's \"no npm refresh exists\" claim is actually true for every npm lockfile filename, not just the one example given.\n\nApply your standard adversarial pass/fail standard: every acceptance criterion testable, no vague language, no TBDs, error cases covered with is_error_case: true, scope narrow enough for one planning cycle. Default disposition is fail. Output a verdict@1 with artifact_type \"spec@1\" and retry_count 2."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":826,"cache_read_input_tokens":609253,"output_tokens":1634,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":826,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1634,"cache_read_input_tokens":609253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":826},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce91GHAwVyZvQ7PeiNxW7","type":"assistant","uuid":"1239457f-b0bc-424c-81b6-e5b5a92b0684","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:09:27.752Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
