xed.** `VersionPlan` carries no group attribution (`plan.rs:14-26`, `45-55`); `lockfile_refresh_results` and `staged` are the real public fields (`apply.rs:406`, `469`).\n\n### Why it still fails: three blockers, all on the AC-002 / AC-002b pair\n\n**1. AC-002b asserts on a non-observable internal call.** Its proposition is that `current_version()` returns `Ok(..)` rather than `Err(ManifestError::WorkspaceInherited)`. That's a `Manifest`-trait call inside `plan_version`; its `Result` never reaches a caller. The spec's own non_goals item 13 binds tests to `plan_version`/`apply_version_plan` as entry points — so AC-002b asserts something its own mandated entry point cannot evaluate. This is the identical defect class I failed AC-011 for one round ago, reintroduced by the edit that fixed AC-011. It also never states what `PlatformWrite.from` must equal — the one value the criterion exists to pin.\n\nThe underlying behavior is real and worth a criterion: `cargo.rs:79-87` errors only when `uses_inheritance &amp;&amp; ctx.cargo_workspace.is_none()`, `cargo.rs:178-189` returns `Ok(v.clone())` when inheritance carries a version, and `WorkspaceInheritance.version` comes from `[workspace.package] version` (`cargo.rs:580-587`). So AC-002b's *scenario* resolves correctly — only its *phrasing* is unusable. Exact replacement text supplied.\n\n**2. AC-002's headline sentence is false in AC-002b's scenario.** It says `from` \"equals the version string currently declared in the platform manifest file at path P.\" When P declares `version.workspace = true` there is no version string in P at all — `cargo.rs:191-199`'s `[package].version` lookup is never reached on that branch. AC-002 and AC-002b give contradictory accounts of where `from` originates. The later mechanism clause resolves it in the intended direction, but a tester applying AC-002 literally to the AC-002b fixture would mark it failed.\n\n**3. AC-002b cites a nonexistent file.** `crates/callisto-graph/src/cargo.rs` does not exist — that directory has no `cargo.rs`. The correct path is `crates/callisto-manifests/src/cargo.rs`, where lines 47-52 are exactly the `inherited_version` detection described.\n\n### Note on one thing I flagged then withdrew\n\nThe `purpose` field still says the lockfile is \"refreshed/staged like any other bump,\" which the summary said was corrected only in `api_surface`. I nearly raised it as a residual instance of blocker 1, then withdrew: the purpose covers both napi-rs (npm) and maturin (Cargo) packages, and for a Cargo platform manifest the lockfile genuinely *is* refreshed via `cargo update --workspace`. Across both ecosystems the phrase is loose but not false.\n\nScope remains one planning cycle — the AC-009 rewrite removed the only scope-explosion path. All three blockers are single-edit fixes with exact replacement text; no follow-up question needed. Next fail would be retry_count 3; escalation triggers above that.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>94953</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>365390</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"e71e2bff-8dc9-4425-ac8d-94a39a6f7699","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:15:38.167Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
