{"parentUuid":"2153572f-aeaa-4645-b237-639fa1caa8af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce936NvRJ1fTZ3AEo46KX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan wasn't written to a scratchpad file — I need to reconstruct it from the notification content and write it to disk myself."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":650614,"output_tokens":10803,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10803,"cache_read_input_tokens":650614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce936JupYbrGfZSEdFbLG","type":"assistant","uuid":"a93bf1fe-5dc8-456b-a6ac-ff5536b64661","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:33:13.090Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"a93bf1fe-5dc8-456b-a6ac-ff5536b64661","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ce936NvRJ1fTZ3AEo46KX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016541byogjGwcgEtBkcZkLA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json","content":"{\n  \"schema\": \"plan@1\",\n  \"id\": \"PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:a8d8b1914557f3af4197f9cfa39333cf6303215d2d28ef4c4a0b092eb6f0785e\",\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified live code before decomposing: PlatformWrite/OptionalDepUpdate are 2-field structs at plan.rs:45-55; plan_version hardcodes both to Vec::new() at version.rs:262-263; apply.rs's platform_writes loop (244-252) has no precondition and active_ecosystems (325-349) only reads plan.bumps. GroupMember::PlatformManifest{owner,role,path,name} lives at config/groups.rs:26-33 and is only populated via IdentityIndex.platform, itself populated in walk.rs:190-216 by detecting npm package.json files with non-empty os+cpu arrays (detect_npm_role, walk.rs:590+) during the walk -- so a realistic test fixture for a Fixed group with a PlatformManifest member is: an owner Cargo crate + a sibling npm package.json declaring os/cpu arrays, referenced by its own npm name in [[fixed-group]] members. Manifest reads go through callisto_manifests::open(&ManifestDecl::new(path, ManifestRole::Canonical, fmt), &OpenContext) exactly as apply.rs already does at 118-136/244-262 -- OpenContext derivation is duplicated verbatim into plan_version rather than extracted into a shared helper, since the spec's api_surface explicitly describes plan_version deriving it itself and extracting a helper is an unrequested refactor. AC-008's 'manifest doesn't exist / can't be parsed' is only reachable at plan_version's read time (not at walk/group-resolution time, since IdentityIndex only ever registers manifests that walked successfully) -- so its test loads a valid workspace first, then removes the platform manifest from disk before calling plan_version, exercising the same code path a real deleted-file race would hit. Tasks are ordered so PlatformWrite's `from` field (Task 1) lands before apply.rs's Fix 2 precondition (Task 8), which is the only cross-file ordering constraint the spec's api_surface calls out; the two commands/version.rs producer sub-features (platform_writes in Tasks 2-4, optional_dep_updates in Tasks 5-6) and the two apply.rs fixes (Tasks 7-8) are otherwise independent of each other by file. Every task's covers_criteria was cross-checked against all 16 IDs (AC-001..AC-013 + AC-002b, AC-007b, AC-012b) at the end -- all 16 present.\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-1\",\n      \"title\": \"Add `from: Version` field to PlatformWrite\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"PlatformWrite is currently a 2-field struct (manifest, version) at plan.rs:45-49. This is a breaking type change that every other task in this plan (Task 2's producer, Task 8's precondition check) depends on. The one existing call site that constructs PlatformWrite directly is the test at apply.rs:2260 (apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates) -- it will fail to compile once the field is added, so it must be fixed in this same task to keep the crate compiling.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"New unit test in plan.rs asserting PlatformWrite has a `from` field. This test does not compile against the current 2-field struct, which is the required RED state for a struct-field addition.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs\",\n        \"code\": \"#[cfg(test)]\\nmod platform_write_from_field_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n    use callisto_model::VersionGrammar;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn platform_write_carries_from_field_distinct_from_version() {\\n        let pw = PlatformWrite {\\n            manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"),\\n            version: Version::parse(\\\"1.1.0\\\", VersionGrammar::SemVer).unwrap(),\\n            from: Version::parse(\\\"1.0.0\\\", VersionGrammar::SemVer).unwrap(),\\n        };\\n        assert_eq!(pw.from.render(), \\\"1.0.0\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(pw.version.render(), \\\"1.1.0\\\");\\n    }\\n}\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib plan::platform_write_from_field_tests\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"error[E0560] or E0609: struct `PlatformWrite` has no field named `from` -- compile error, crate fails to build\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add the `from` field to PlatformWrite, then fix the one pre-existing direct constructor at apply.rs:2260 so the crate compiles.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs, change `pub struct PlatformWrite { pub manifest: PathBuf, pub version: Version }` to `pub struct PlatformWrite { pub manifest: PathBuf, pub version: Version, pub from: Version }`.\",\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, in the test `apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates` (around line 2260), change the `PlatformWrite` literal from `crate::plan::PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"), version: cargo_version(\\\"1.1.0\\\") }` to `crate::plan::PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"), version: cargo_version(\\\"1.1.0\\\"), from: cargo_version(\\\"1.0.0\\\") }` -- 1.0.0 matches the fixture's on-disk platform/package.json version, so this remains the non-drifted, non-precondition-failing case.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including plan::platform_write_from_field_tests::platform_write_carries_from_field_distinct_from_version and apply::tests::apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): add `from` field to PlatformWrite\\n\\nCaptures the platform manifest's on-disk version at plan time so apply_version_plan can precondition-check it before writing, mirroring PlannedBump.from's role in the sibling bump loops.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-2\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version: OpenContext derivation + core platform_writes producer (single platform member, happy path)\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-1\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"This is the core producer logic: for each Fixed group's GroupMember::PlatformManifest whose owner received a real PlannedBump this run, open the platform manifest (ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, OpenContext derived exactly as apply.rs:118-130 does) and emit a PlatformWrite with from=on-disk current_version, version=owner's bump target. Also covers the two 'no write should happen' regressions (AC-005: no platform members anywhere; AC-006: owner not bumped) since they exercise the same new code path with zero/no-match inputs and share the test fixture helpers already in this file's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` (git_init_with_commit, tag, commit_all).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Three tests added to commands/version.rs's existing test module, reusing its git_init_with_commit/tag/commit_all helpers. Platform manifest fixtures use a Cargo owner package plus a sibling npm package.json with non-empty os/cpu arrays (the only mechanism, per walk.rs:590-630, that causes IdentityIndex to register a GroupMember::PlatformManifest), referenced in [[fixed-group]] members by its own npm package name.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_bumped_owner_with_platform_sibling commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_writes_empty_when_no_platform_members_exist commands::version::tests::plan_version_no_platform_write_when_owner_not_bumped\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_bumped_owner_with_platform_sibling fails: assertion `left == right` failed: expected exactly one PlatformWrite, got: [] (plan_version currently hardcodes platform_writes to Vec::new()). The other two tests pass trivially before implementation since Vec::new() is already empty -- they exist to pin the regression once the producer logic is added.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Replace the hardcoded `platform_writes: Vec::new()` with real producer logic, driven by Fixed-group PlatformManifest members whose owner has an entry in the `bumps` vector already computed earlier in this function.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"Add `use crate::config::groups::{GroupMember, GroupMemberKind};` to the top of crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs.\",\n          \"Immediately before the `Ok(VersionPlan { ... })` return at the end of plan_version, derive cargo_workspace/npm_workspace_kind/OpenContext exactly as apply.rs:118-130 does, then loop over ws.config.groups.fixed.values() -> group.members(GroupMemberKind::PlatformManifest), and for each owner with an entry in bump_by_pkg, open the manifest via ManifestFormat::from_path + ManifestDecl::new(path, ManifestRole::Canonical, fmt) + callisto_manifests::open(&decl, &open_ctx), read current_version(), and push a PlatformWrite { manifest: path.clone(), version: bump.to.clone(), from: current }.\",\n          \"Change the VersionPlan struct literal's `platform_writes: Vec::new(),` to `platform_writes,` (the newly computed variable). Leave `optional_dep_updates: Vec::new(),` untouched for this task -- Task 5 replaces it.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including the three new tests\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): produce real PlatformWrite entries in plan_version\\n\\nplan_version now walks Fixed-group PlatformManifest members whose owner has a real PlannedBump this run, reads each platform manifest's current on-disk version via the same OpenContext derivation apply_version_plan already uses, and emits a PlatformWrite carrying both from and target version -- closing the previously hardcoded Vec::new() gap.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-001\", \"AC-002\", \"AC-005\", \"AC-006\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-3\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version platform_writes: workspace-inherited Cargo version + multiple platform siblings\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Task 2's implementation already derives cargo_workspace inheritance into OpenContext and opens manifests via ManifestRole::Canonical regardless of format, so a `version.workspace = true` Cargo platform manifest and multiple platform siblings under one owner both flow through the same code path with zero additional implementation. This task adds tests only, pinning that these two scenarios genuinely work end-to-end through plan_version's real return value (not a direct current_version() call in isolation, per AC-002b's wording).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Two tests: AC-002b (maturin-style Cargo platform manifest inheriting version.workspace = true from the root [workspace.package] version) and AC-007 (owner with two platform siblings, both must appear).\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings fails before Task 2's implementation lands (platform_writes hardcoded empty); after Task 2, both tests should already pass with zero further implementation changes -- if either fails after Task 2, the implementation has a gap (only one platform member being processed, or the cargo_workspace inheritance not reaching the correct WorkspaceInheritance).\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- Task 2's loop already iterates every PlatformManifest member per group and already derives cargo_workspace inheritance into OpenContext. This task exists purely to pin the two scenarios with dedicated tests, per the spec's explicit call-out that both must be proven through plan_version's actual return value.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"No production code changes. If either test fails, the bug is in Task 2's implementation (loop only processing the first PlatformManifest member found, or cargo_workspace being derived as None instead of from WorkspaceCargoResolver) -- fix that code in commands/version.rs rather than adding new code here.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-002b workspace-inherited Cargo platform version and AC-007 multi-sibling platform writes\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-002b\", \"AC-007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-4\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version platform_writes: AC-008 error propagation on unreadable platform manifest\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Task 2's implementation already uses `?` on ManifestFormat::from_path, ManifestDecl::new, callisto_manifests::open, and current_version() -- all of which already propagate as GraphError. This test proves that end-to-end: a platform manifest that validated during the walk (so it is a real GroupMember::PlatformManifest) but is deleted from disk before plan_version runs must surface as Err, not panic and not a partial VersionPlan.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Build a valid workspace with a platform member (walk succeeds, group resolves), load the Workspace, then delete the platform manifest file from disk before calling plan_version -- simulating the file having gone missing between workspace load and plan execution.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_missing_from_disk_at_plan_time\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"Before Task 2's implementation exists, this test fails because plan_version succeeds with an empty platform_writes (the hardcoded Vec::new() never reads the manifest at all, so nothing errors). Since this task depends on Task 2, in practice this test is written and should pass immediately once Task 2 is merged -- if it does not, Task 2's `?` propagation has a gap and must be fixed there.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- Task 2's `?`-based propagation on open()/current_version() already produces this behavior. This task is test-only, confirming the error path.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"No production code changes required. If the test fails, fix the propagation gap in Task 2's loop in commands/version.rs (commonly: a `.ok()` or `.unwrap_or_default()` silently swallowing the error instead of `?`).\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-008 error propagation for platform manifest missing at plan_version read time\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-5\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version: optional_dep_updates producer (single platform member)\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Extends the same group/member loop from Task 2: for each platform member whose owner was bumped, additionally open the owner's own canonical manifest and check via iter_dependencies() whether an existing DepKind::Optional entry matches the platform member's name. Only when a match exists is an OptionalDepUpdate produced -- never speculatively created (AC-004).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"AC-003 (owner has a matching optionalDependencies entry -> update produced) and AC-004 (owner has no matching entry -> nothing produced) as two tests.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_optional_dep_update_when_owner_declares_matching_optional_dep commands::version::tests::plan_version_no_optional_dep_update_when_owner_has_no_matching_dependency\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_emits_optional_dep_update_when_owner_declares_matching_optional_dep fails: assertion `left == right` failed: got: [] (optional_dep_updates is still hardcoded to Vec::new() before this task's implementation lands).\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Extend the loop added in Task 2 to also detect a matching optional dependency on the owner's canonical manifest and accumulate updates per owner-manifest-path (using a BTreeMap so multiple platform siblings under the same owner naturally merge, which Task 6 pins).\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In the same loop from Task 2, also bind `name` from the GroupMember::PlatformManifest destructure.\",\n          \"Before the loop, add a `BTreeMap<PathBuf, Vec<(String, Version)>>` accumulator for optional dep updates.\",\n          \"Inside the loop, after computing `bump`, open the owner's canonical manifest and check via iter_dependencies() whether a DepKind::Optional entry matches `name`; if so, push (name, bump.to) into the accumulator keyed by the owner's manifest path.\",\n          \"After the loop, convert the accumulator into Vec<OptionalDepUpdate> and assign it to the VersionPlan struct literal's `optional_dep_updates` field, replacing `Vec::new()`.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): produce real OptionalDepUpdate entries in plan_version\\n\\nWhen a Fixed group's owner package declares an existing optionalDependencies entry matching a bumped platform-manifest sibling's name, plan_version now emits an OptionalDepUpdate targeting that entry -- never speculatively creating one that didn't already exist.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-003\", \"AC-004\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-6\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version optional_dep_updates: AC-007b merge behavior for two platform siblings\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-5\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Task 5's implementation already keys optional_dep_map by owner manifest path and pushes into the same Vec on repeated inserts (BTreeMap::entry(...).or_default().push(...)), so two platform siblings under one owner naturally merge into a single OptionalDepUpdate rather than producing two entries pointing at the same manifest. This task pins that behavior with a dedicated test; no new implementation is needed.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Owner with two platform siblings, both with matching optionalDependencies entries on the owner's manifest -- exactly one OptionalDepUpdate for the owner's path, containing both (name, version) pairs.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_merges_two_platform_siblings_optional_dep_updates_into_one_entry\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"Depends on Task 5 being complete; if Task 5's map keying is wrong (e.g. keyed per-member instead of per-owner-manifest-path), this fails with `plan.optional_dep_updates.len() == 2` instead of 1.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- Task 5's BTreeMap<PathBuf, Vec<...>>::entry(...).or_default().push(...) pattern already merges by manifest path.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"No production code changes required. If the test fails, fix Task 5's optional_dep_map keying in commands/version.rs so it is keyed by owner canonical manifest path, not per-platform-member.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-007b merged optional_dep_updates for two platform siblings under one owner\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-007b\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-7\",\n      \"title\": \"apply.rs Fix 1: extend active_ecosystems to platform_writes and optional_dep_updates manifest paths\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"active_ecosystems (apply.rs:325-349) currently only derives from plan.bumps, so a plan with only platform_writes/optional_dep_updates populated (bumps empty) never stages the npm lockfile even though an npm manifest was touched. This task extends the same active_ecosystems HashSet-building expression to also fold in plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates manifest paths via ManifestFormat::from_path(...).ecosystem(). This task is independent of Tasks 1-6 (different file, does not touch PlatformWrite's fields) and independent of Task 8 (no precondition logic involved) -- it can be built and merged in any order relative to them.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"AC-009 (platform_writes-only plan stages the npm lockfile, no refresh), AC-010 (same for optional_dep_updates-only plan), AC-011 (bumps-only plan behavior is a byte-for-byte regression -- already covered by every pre-existing apply.rs test in this file, which all currently pass and must continue to pass unmodified).\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib apply::tests::platform_writes_only_plan_stages_npm_lockfile_without_refresh apply::tests::optional_dep_updates_only_plan_stages_npm_lockfile_without_refresh\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"Both tests fail: `assert!(outcome.staged.contains(...))` fails because active_ecosystems is currently derived only from plan.bumps (empty in both plans), so Ecosystem::Npm is never in the set and the lockfile is skipped in the staging loop at apply.rs:423-431.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Extend the active_ecosystems HashSet-building code (apply.rs:325-349) to also fold in manifest paths from plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, chain two additional filter_map iterators onto the existing active_ecosystems collect(): one over plan.platform_writes mapping each pw.manifest through ManifestFormat::from_path(...).ok().map(|fmt| fmt.ecosystem()), and one over plan.optional_dep_updates doing the same for opt.manifest.\",\n          \"No other code changes -- the existing lockfile_ecosystems staging table (apply.rs:412-422) and refresh-subprocess logic (apply.rs:354-408) are untouched, since npm has no refresh subprocess and Cargo/Pypi refresh triggers stay scoped to plan.bumps-driven ecosystems only.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including all pre-existing apply.rs tests (proving AC-011's byte-for-byte regression requirement)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): stage npm lockfile when a plan touches only platform_writes or optional_dep_updates\\n\\nactive_ecosystems previously derived exclusively from plan.bumps, so a plan containing only platform-manifest or optional-dependency writes never staged the npm lockfile. Extends the derivation to also consult those two fields' manifest paths.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-009\", \"AC-010\", \"AC-011\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-8\",\n      \"title\": \"apply.rs Fix 2: platform_writes dispatch loop precondition check\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-1\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The platform_writes dispatch loop (apply.rs:244-252) currently writes unconditionally with no precondition check, unlike the sibling bump loops which already check current==from/current==target/else. This task adds the same three-way branch using PlatformWrite.from (added in Task 1), returning GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion on drift, treating current==target as idempotent-retry success.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Three tests: AC-012 (drift -- current is neither from nor target -> Err(UnexpectedManifestVersion) with correct fields, manifest not written), AC-012b (current already equals target -> Ok, no re-write, but path still pushed to staged), AC-013 (current equals from, the ordinary case -> succeeds, on-disk version becomes target -- this is the pre-existing test from apply.rs:2240, already updated with a matching `from` in Task 1, and must continue to pass unmodified as the regression proof).\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib apply::tests::platform_write_drift_returns_unexpected_manifest_version_and_leaves_manifest_untouched apply::tests::platform_write_idempotent_retry_when_already_at_target_succeeds_without_rewrite\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"platform_write_drift_returns_unexpected_manifest_version_and_leaves_manifest_untouched fails: `apply_version_plan` currently succeeds unconditionally (writes 1.1.0 over the drifted 9.9.9), so `result` is `Ok(..)` not `Err(UnexpectedManifestVersion)`, and the manifest is NOT unchanged. platform_write_idempotent_retry_when_already_at_target_succeeds_without_rewrite happens to pass even before the fix (current unconditional-write behavior also succeeds here), but is included to pin AC-012b's exact non-error semantics once the precondition check exists.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add the same three-way current==from/current==to/else branch the sibling bump loops already use, to the platform_writes dispatch loop.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, in the platform_writes loop (currently around lines 244-252), after opening the handle, read current_version(), then branch: if current == pw.version, skip the write (idempotent retry) but still push to modified_paths; else if current == pw.from, write_version + persist as before; else, return Err(GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion { path: pw.manifest.clone(), expected_from: pw.from.clone(), expected_to: pw.version.clone(), found: current }).\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including the pre-existing apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates test (proving AC-013's non-drifted regression path)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): add current-version precondition check to platform_writes dispatch loop\\n\\napply_version_plan previously wrote platform manifests unconditionally, unlike the sibling bump loops. Adds the same current==from/current==to/else precondition, returning UnexpectedManifestVersion on drift and treating current==to as a safe idempotent-retry success.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-012\", \"AC-012b\", \"AC-013\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria_coverage_check\": {\n    \"AC-001\": [\"TASK-2\"], \"AC-002\": [\"TASK-2\"], \"AC-002b\": [\"TASK-3\"],\n    \"AC-003\": [\"TASK-5\"], \"AC-004\": [\"TASK-5\"], \"AC-005\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n    \"AC-006\": [\"TASK-2\"], \"AC-007\": [\"TASK-3\"], \"AC-007b\": [\"TASK-6\"],\n    \"AC-008\": [\"TASK-4\"], \"AC-009\": [\"TASK-7\"], \"AC-010\": [\"TASK-7\"],\n    \"AC-011\": [\"TASK-7\"], \"AC-012\": [\"TASK-8\"], \"AC-012b\": [\"TASK-8\"],\n    \"AC-013\": [\"TASK-8\"]\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":650614,"output_tokens":10803,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":10803,"cache_read_input_tokens":650614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":375},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce936JupYbrGfZSEdFbLG","type":"assistant","uuid":"1e658f2e-afc4-44f4-842d-c98ff1d35e15","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:34:24.430Z","effort":"high","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
{"parentUuid":"1e658f2e-afc4-44f4-842d-c98ff1d35e15","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ff273322-5bdc-4fd9-a704-4b145e80ebb3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016541byogjGwcgEtBkcZkLA","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"150dd552-e110-4fb8-8b72-767c09811fe2","timestamp":"2026-08-17T21:34:29.261Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto/.claude/plans/PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json","content":"{\n  \"schema\": \"plan@1\",\n  \"id\": \"PLAN-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n  \"spec_file_path\": \".claude/specs/SPEC-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES.json\",\n  \"spec_hash\": \"sha256:a8d8b1914557f3af4197f9cfa39333cf6303215d2d28ef4c4a0b092eb6f0785e\",\n  \"linked_requirement\": \"REQ-TRACK2-PLATFORM-MANIFEST-WRITES\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"Verified live code before decomposing: PlatformWrite/OptionalDepUpdate are 2-field structs at plan.rs:45-55; plan_version hardcodes both to Vec::new() at version.rs:262-263; apply.rs's platform_writes loop (244-252) has no precondition and active_ecosystems (325-349) only reads plan.bumps. GroupMember::PlatformManifest{owner,role,path,name} lives at config/groups.rs:26-33 and is only populated via IdentityIndex.platform, itself populated in walk.rs:190-216 by detecting npm package.json files with non-empty os+cpu arrays (detect_npm_role, walk.rs:590+) during the walk -- so a realistic test fixture for a Fixed group with a PlatformManifest member is: an owner Cargo crate + a sibling npm package.json declaring os/cpu arrays, referenced by its own npm name in [[fixed-group]] members. Manifest reads go through callisto_manifests::open(&ManifestDecl::new(path, ManifestRole::Canonical, fmt), &OpenContext) exactly as apply.rs already does at 118-136/244-262 -- OpenContext derivation is duplicated verbatim into plan_version rather than extracted into a shared helper, since the spec's api_surface explicitly describes plan_version deriving it itself and extracting a helper is an unrequested refactor. AC-008's 'manifest doesn't exist / can't be parsed' is only reachable at plan_version's read time (not at walk/group-resolution time, since IdentityIndex only ever registers manifests that walked successfully) -- so its test loads a valid workspace first, then removes the platform manifest from disk before calling plan_version, exercising the same code path a real deleted-file race would hit. Tasks are ordered so PlatformWrite's `from` field (Task 1) lands before apply.rs's Fix 2 precondition (Task 8), which is the only cross-file ordering constraint the spec's api_surface calls out; the two commands/version.rs producer sub-features (platform_writes in Tasks 2-4, optional_dep_updates in Tasks 5-6) and the two apply.rs fixes (Tasks 7-8) are otherwise independent of each other by file. Every task's covers_criteria was cross-checked against all 16 IDs (AC-001..AC-013 + AC-002b, AC-007b, AC-012b) at the end -- all 16 present.\",\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-1\",\n      \"title\": \"Add `from: Version` field to PlatformWrite\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs\", \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"PlatformWrite is currently a 2-field struct (manifest, version) at plan.rs:45-49. This is a breaking type change that every other task in this plan (Task 2's producer, Task 8's precondition check) depends on. The one existing call site that constructs PlatformWrite directly is the test at apply.rs:2260 (apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates) -- it will fail to compile once the field is added, so it must be fixed in this same task to keep the crate compiling.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"New unit test in plan.rs asserting PlatformWrite has a `from` field. This test does not compile against the current 2-field struct, which is the required RED state for a struct-field addition.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs\",\n        \"code\": \"#[cfg(test)]\\nmod platform_write_from_field_tests {\\n    use super::*;\\n    use callisto_model::VersionGrammar;\\n\\n    #[test]\\n    fn platform_write_carries_from_field_distinct_from_version() {\\n        let pw = PlatformWrite {\\n            manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"),\\n            version: Version::parse(\\\"1.1.0\\\", VersionGrammar::SemVer).unwrap(),\\n            from: Version::parse(\\\"1.0.0\\\", VersionGrammar::SemVer).unwrap(),\\n        };\\n        assert_eq!(pw.from.render(), \\\"1.0.0\\\");\\n        assert_eq!(pw.version.render(), \\\"1.1.0\\\");\\n    }\\n}\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib plan::platform_write_from_field_tests\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"error[E0560] or E0609: struct `PlatformWrite` has no field named `from` -- compile error, crate fails to build\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add the `from` field to PlatformWrite, then fix the one pre-existing direct constructor at apply.rs:2260 so the crate compiles.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/plan.rs, change `pub struct PlatformWrite { pub manifest: PathBuf, pub version: Version }` to `pub struct PlatformWrite { pub manifest: PathBuf, pub version: Version, pub from: Version }`.\",\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, in the test `apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates` (around line 2260), change the `PlatformWrite` literal from `crate::plan::PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"), version: cargo_version(\\\"1.1.0\\\") }` to `crate::plan::PlatformWrite { manifest: PathBuf::from(\\\"platform/package.json\\\"), version: cargo_version(\\\"1.1.0\\\"), from: cargo_version(\\\"1.0.0\\\") }` -- 1.0.0 matches the fixture's on-disk platform/package.json version, so this remains the non-drifted, non-precondition-failing case.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including plan::platform_write_from_field_tests::platform_write_carries_from_field_distinct_from_version and apply::tests::apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): add `from` field to PlatformWrite\\n\\nCaptures the platform manifest's on-disk version at plan time so apply_version_plan can precondition-check it before writing, mirroring PlannedBump.from's role in the sibling bump loops.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-2\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version: OpenContext derivation + core platform_writes producer (single platform member, happy path)\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-1\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"This is the core producer logic: for each Fixed group's GroupMember::PlatformManifest whose owner received a real PlannedBump this run, open the platform manifest (ManifestRole::Canonical unconditionally, OpenContext derived exactly as apply.rs:118-130 does) and emit a PlatformWrite with from=on-disk current_version, version=owner's bump target. Also covers the two 'no write should happen' regressions (AC-005: no platform members anywhere; AC-006: owner not bumped) since they exercise the same new code path with zero/no-match inputs and share the test fixture helpers already in this file's `#[cfg(test)] mod tests` (git_init_with_commit, tag, commit_all).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Three tests added to commands/version.rs's existing test module, reusing its git_init_with_commit/tag/commit_all helpers. Platform manifest fixtures use a Cargo owner package plus a sibling npm package.json with non-empty os/cpu arrays (the only mechanism, per walk.rs:590-630, that causes IdentityIndex to register a GroupMember::PlatformManifest), referenced in [[fixed-group]] members by its own npm package name.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_bumped_owner_with_platform_sibling commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_writes_empty_when_no_platform_members_exist commands::version::tests::plan_version_no_platform_write_when_owner_not_bumped\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_bumped_owner_with_platform_sibling fails: assertion `left == right` failed: expected exactly one PlatformWrite, got: [] (plan_version currently hardcodes platform_writes to Vec::new()). The other two tests pass trivially before implementation since Vec::new() is already empty -- they exist to pin the regression once the producer logic is added.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Replace the hardcoded `platform_writes: Vec::new()` with real producer logic, driven by Fixed-group PlatformManifest members whose owner has an entry in the `bumps` vector already computed earlier in this function.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"Add `use crate::config::groups::{GroupMember, GroupMemberKind};` to the top of crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs.\",\n          \"Immediately before the `Ok(VersionPlan { ... })` return at the end of plan_version, derive cargo_workspace/npm_workspace_kind/OpenContext exactly as apply.rs:118-130 does, then loop over ws.config.groups.fixed.values() -> group.members(GroupMemberKind::PlatformManifest), and for each owner with an entry in bump_by_pkg, open the manifest via ManifestFormat::from_path + ManifestDecl::new(path, ManifestRole::Canonical, fmt) + callisto_manifests::open(&decl, &open_ctx), read current_version(), and push a PlatformWrite { manifest: path.clone(), version: bump.to.clone(), from: current }.\",\n          \"Change the VersionPlan struct literal's `platform_writes: Vec::new(),` to `platform_writes,` (the newly computed variable). Leave `optional_dep_updates: Vec::new(),` untouched for this task -- Task 5 replaces it.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including the three new tests\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): produce real PlatformWrite entries in plan_version\\n\\nplan_version now walks Fixed-group PlatformManifest members whose owner has a real PlannedBump this run, reads each platform manifest's current on-disk version via the same OpenContext derivation apply_version_plan already uses, and emits a PlatformWrite carrying both from and target version -- closing the previously hardcoded Vec::new() gap.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-001\", \"AC-002\", \"AC-005\", \"AC-006\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-3\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version platform_writes: workspace-inherited Cargo version + multiple platform siblings\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Task 2's implementation already derives cargo_workspace inheritance into OpenContext and opens manifests via ManifestRole::Canonical regardless of format, so a `version.workspace = true` Cargo platform manifest and multiple platform siblings under one owner both flow through the same code path with zero additional implementation. This task adds tests only, pinning that these two scenarios genuinely work end-to-end through plan_version's real return value (not a direct current_version() call in isolation, per AC-002b's wording).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Two tests: AC-002b (maturin-style Cargo platform manifest inheriting version.workspace = true from the root [workspace.package] version) and AC-007 (owner with two platform siblings, both must appear).\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_platform_write_from_resolves_cargo_workspace_inherited_version commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_emits_platform_write_for_each_of_two_platform_siblings fails before Task 2's implementation lands (platform_writes hardcoded empty); after Task 2, both tests should already pass with zero further implementation changes -- if either fails after Task 2, the implementation has a gap (only one platform member being processed, or the cargo_workspace inheritance not reaching the correct WorkspaceInheritance).\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- Task 2's loop already iterates every PlatformManifest member per group and already derives cargo_workspace inheritance into OpenContext. This task exists purely to pin the two scenarios with dedicated tests, per the spec's explicit call-out that both must be proven through plan_version's actual return value.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"No production code changes. If either test fails, the bug is in Task 2's implementation (loop only processing the first PlatformManifest member found, or cargo_workspace being derived as None instead of from WorkspaceCargoResolver) -- fix that code in commands/version.rs rather than adding new code here.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-002b workspace-inherited Cargo platform version and AC-007 multi-sibling platform writes\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-002b\", \"AC-007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-4\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version platform_writes: AC-008 error propagation on unreadable platform manifest\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Task 2's implementation already uses `?` on ManifestFormat::from_path, ManifestDecl::new, callisto_manifests::open, and current_version() -- all of which already propagate as GraphError. This test proves that end-to-end: a platform manifest that validated during the walk (so it is a real GroupMember::PlatformManifest) but is deleted from disk before plan_version runs must surface as Err, not panic and not a partial VersionPlan.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Build a valid workspace with a platform member (walk succeeds, group resolves), load the Workspace, then delete the platform manifest file from disk before calling plan_version -- simulating the file having gone missing between workspace load and plan execution.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_returns_err_when_platform_manifest_missing_from_disk_at_plan_time\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"Before Task 2's implementation exists, this test fails because plan_version succeeds with an empty platform_writes (the hardcoded Vec::new() never reads the manifest at all, so nothing errors). Since this task depends on Task 2, in practice this test is written and should pass immediately once Task 2 is merged -- if it does not, Task 2's `?` propagation has a gap and must be fixed there.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- Task 2's `?`-based propagation on open()/current_version() already produces this behavior. This task is test-only, confirming the error path.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"No production code changes required. If the test fails, fix the propagation gap in Task 2's loop in commands/version.rs (commonly: a `.ok()` or `.unwrap_or_default()` silently swallowing the error instead of `?`).\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-008 error propagation for platform manifest missing at plan_version read time\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-5\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version: optional_dep_updates producer (single platform member)\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Extends the same group/member loop from Task 2: for each platform member whose owner was bumped, additionally open the owner's own canonical manifest and check via iter_dependencies() whether an existing DepKind::Optional entry matches the platform member's name. Only when a match exists is an OptionalDepUpdate produced -- never speculatively created (AC-004).\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"AC-003 (owner has a matching optionalDependencies entry -> update produced) and AC-004 (owner has no matching entry -> nothing produced) as two tests.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_emits_optional_dep_update_when_owner_declares_matching_optional_dep commands::version::tests::plan_version_no_optional_dep_update_when_owner_has_no_matching_dependency\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"plan_version_emits_optional_dep_update_when_owner_declares_matching_optional_dep fails: assertion `left == right` failed: got: [] (optional_dep_updates is still hardcoded to Vec::new() before this task's implementation lands).\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Extend the loop added in Task 2 to also detect a matching optional dependency on the owner's canonical manifest and accumulate updates per owner-manifest-path (using a BTreeMap so multiple platform siblings under the same owner naturally merge, which Task 6 pins).\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In the same loop from Task 2, also bind `name` from the GroupMember::PlatformManifest destructure.\",\n          \"Before the loop, add a `BTreeMap<PathBuf, Vec<(String, Version)>>` accumulator for optional dep updates.\",\n          \"Inside the loop, after computing `bump`, open the owner's canonical manifest and check via iter_dependencies() whether a DepKind::Optional entry matches `name`; if so, push (name, bump.to) into the accumulator keyed by the owner's manifest path.\",\n          \"After the loop, convert the accumulator into Vec<OptionalDepUpdate> and assign it to the VersionPlan struct literal's `optional_dep_updates` field, replacing `Vec::new()`.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"feat(graph): produce real OptionalDepUpdate entries in plan_version\\n\\nWhen a Fixed group's owner package declares an existing optionalDependencies entry matching a bumped platform-manifest sibling's name, plan_version now emits an OptionalDepUpdate targeting that entry -- never speculatively creating one that didn't already exist.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-003\", \"AC-004\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-6\",\n      \"title\": \"plan_version optional_dep_updates: AC-007b merge behavior for two platform siblings\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-5\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Task 5's implementation already keys optional_dep_map by owner manifest path and pushes into the same Vec on repeated inserts (BTreeMap::entry(...).or_default().push(...)), so two platform siblings under one owner naturally merge into a single OptionalDepUpdate rather than producing two entries pointing at the same manifest. This task pins that behavior with a dedicated test; no new implementation is needed.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Owner with two platform siblings, both with matching optionalDependencies entries on the owner's manifest -- exactly one OptionalDepUpdate for the owner's path, containing both (name, version) pairs.\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/version.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib commands::version::tests::plan_version_merges_two_platform_siblings_optional_dep_updates_into_one_entry\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"Depends on Task 5 being complete; if Task 5's map keying is wrong (e.g. keyed per-member instead of per-owner-manifest-path), this fails with `plan.optional_dep_updates.len() == 2` instead of 1.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"No new implementation code -- Task 5's BTreeMap<PathBuf, Vec<...>>::entry(...).or_default().push(...) pattern already merges by manifest path.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"No production code changes required. If the test fails, fix Task 5's optional_dep_map keying in commands/version.rs so it is keyed by owner canonical manifest path, not per-platform-member.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"test(graph): pin AC-007b merged optional_dep_updates for two platform siblings under one owner\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-007b\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-7\",\n      \"title\": \"apply.rs Fix 1: extend active_ecosystems to platform_writes and optional_dep_updates manifest paths\",\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"active_ecosystems (apply.rs:325-349) currently only derives from plan.bumps, so a plan with only platform_writes/optional_dep_updates populated (bumps empty) never stages the npm lockfile even though an npm manifest was touched. This task extends the same active_ecosystems HashSet-building expression to also fold in plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates manifest paths via ManifestFormat::from_path(...).ecosystem(). This task is independent of Tasks 1-6 (different file, does not touch PlatformWrite's fields) and independent of Task 8 (no precondition logic involved) -- it can be built and merged in any order relative to them.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"AC-009 (platform_writes-only plan stages the npm lockfile, no refresh), AC-010 (same for optional_dep_updates-only plan), AC-011 (bumps-only plan behavior is a byte-for-byte regression -- already covered by every pre-existing apply.rs test in this file, which all currently pass and must continue to pass unmodified).\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib apply::tests::platform_writes_only_plan_stages_npm_lockfile_without_refresh apply::tests::optional_dep_updates_only_plan_stages_npm_lockfile_without_refresh\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"Both tests fail: `assert!(outcome.staged.contains(...))` fails because active_ecosystems is currently derived only from plan.bumps (empty in both plans), so Ecosystem::Npm is never in the set and the lockfile is skipped in the staging loop at apply.rs:423-431.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Extend the active_ecosystems HashSet-building code (apply.rs:325-349) to also fold in manifest paths from plan.platform_writes and plan.optional_dep_updates.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, chain two additional filter_map iterators onto the existing active_ecosystems collect(): one over plan.platform_writes mapping each pw.manifest through ManifestFormat::from_path(...).ok().map(|fmt| fmt.ecosystem()), and one over plan.optional_dep_updates doing the same for opt.manifest.\",\n          \"No other code changes -- the existing lockfile_ecosystems staging table (apply.rs:412-422) and refresh-subprocess logic (apply.rs:354-408) are untouched, since npm has no refresh subprocess and Cargo/Pypi refresh triggers stay scoped to plan.bumps-driven ecosystems only.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including all pre-existing apply.rs tests (proving AC-011's byte-for-byte regression requirement)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): stage npm lockfile when a plan touches only platform_writes or optional_dep_updates\\n\\nactive_ecosystems previously derived exclusively from plan.bumps, so a plan containing only platform-manifest or optional-dependency writes never staged the npm lockfile. Extends the derivation to also consult those two fields' manifest paths.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-009\", \"AC-010\", \"AC-011\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"TASK-8\",\n      \"title\": \"apply.rs Fix 2: platform_writes dispatch loop precondition check\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"TASK-1\"],\n      \"files\": [\"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\"],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The platform_writes dispatch loop (apply.rs:244-252) currently writes unconditionally with no precondition check, unlike the sibling bump loops which already check current==from/current==target/else. This task adds the same three-way branch using PlatformWrite.from (added in Task 1), returning GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion on drift, treating current==target as idempotent-retry success.\",\n      \"test\": {\n        \"description\": \"Three tests: AC-012 (drift -- current is neither from nor target -> Err(UnexpectedManifestVersion) with correct fields, manifest not written), AC-012b (current already equals target -> Ok, no re-write, but path still pushed to staged), AC-013 (current equals from, the ordinary case -> succeeds, on-disk version becomes target -- this is the pre-existing test from apply.rs:2240, already updated with a matching `from` in Task 1, and must continue to pass unmodified as the regression proof).\",\n        \"file\": \"crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs\",\n        \"run_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib apply::tests::platform_write_drift_returns_unexpected_manifest_version_and_leaves_manifest_untouched apply::tests::platform_write_idempotent_retry_when_already_at_target_succeeds_without_rewrite\",\n        \"expected_failure\": \"platform_write_drift_returns_unexpected_manifest_version_and_leaves_manifest_untouched fails: `apply_version_plan` currently succeeds unconditionally (writes 1.1.0 over the drifted 9.9.9), so `result` is `Ok(..)` not `Err(UnexpectedManifestVersion)`, and the manifest is NOT unchanged. platform_write_idempotent_retry_when_already_at_target_succeeds_without_rewrite happens to pass even before the fix (current unconditional-write behavior also succeeds here), but is included to pin AC-012b's exact non-error semantics once the precondition check exists.\"\n      },\n      \"implementation\": {\n        \"description\": \"Add the same three-way current==from/current==to/else branch the sibling bump loops already use, to the platform_writes dispatch loop.\",\n        \"steps\": [\n          \"In crates/callisto-graph/src/apply.rs, in the platform_writes loop (currently around lines 244-252), after opening the handle, read current_version(), then branch: if current == pw.version, skip the write (idempotent retry) but still push to modified_paths; else if current == pw.from, write_version + persist as before; else, return Err(GraphError::UnexpectedManifestVersion { path: pw.manifest.clone(), expected_from: pw.from.clone(), expected_to: pw.version.clone(), found: current }).\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"verify_command\": \"cargo test -p callisto-graph --lib\",\n      \"expected_pass\": \"all tests pass, including the pre-existing apply_version_plan_executes_platform_writes_and_optional_dep_updates test (proving AC-013's non-drifted regression path)\",\n      \"commit_message\": \"fix(graph): add current-version precondition check to platform_writes dispatch loop\\n\\napply_version_plan previously wrote platform manifests unconditionally, unlike the sibling bump loops. Adds the same current==from/current==to/else precondition, returning UnexpectedManifestVersion on drift and treating current==to as a safe idempotent-retry success.\",\n      \"covers_criteria\": [\"AC-012\", \"AC-012b\", \"AC-013\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"criteria_coverage_check\": {\n    \"AC-001\": [\"TASK-2\"], \"AC-002\": [\"TASK-2\"], \"AC-002b\": [\"TASK-3\"],\n    \"AC-003\": [\"TASK-5\"], \"AC-004\": [\"TASK-5\"], \"AC-005\": [\"TASK-2\"],\n    \"AC-006\": [\"TASK-2\"], \"AC-007\": [\"TASK-3\"], \"AC-007b\": [\"TASK-6\"],\n    \"AC-008\": [\"TASK-4\"], \"AC-009\": [\"TASK-7\"], \"AC-010\": [\"TASK-7\"],\n    \"AC-011\": [\"TASK-7\"], \"AC-012\": [\"TASK-8\"], \"AC-012b\": [\"TASK-8\"],\n    \"AC-013\": [\"TASK-8\"]\n  }\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1e658f2e-afc4-44f4-842d-c98ff1d35e15","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
