p, not something this track introduced. The one survivor genuinely inside Track 1's new code (the Fixed-group convergence block's idempotency guard, `cascade.rs:404/407`) exactly mirrors a pre-existing, already-accepted gap in the Linked-group block it deliberately copies (`cascade.rs:333/336`) — consistent with, not worse than, the existing pattern. 25 precision tests were specified by the mutator; deferred as backlog (see Track 11/12-adjacent follow-up), not blocking, since fixing the pre-existing gaps is out of this track's scope and the one in-scope gap matches accepted precedent.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"00b45ad0-a0b2-4a2c-8770-192bf1a451b7","session_id":"bb531e8d-c394-4e47-a8ae-e4a9ceeca6d2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/callisto","sessionId":"ae412d01-e061-4047-918b-0d1df3d4d118","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"shimmying-giggling-hickey"}
